/* === Aral Sea expedition article translations === */
Object.assign(window.I18N.ru, {"Route": "Маршрут", "Day 01": "День 01", "Day 02": "День 02", "Day 03": "День 03", "Day 04": "День 04", "Day 05": "День 05", "Day 06": "День 06", "Day 07": "День 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Полевой дневник · Отчёт об экспедиции · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Семь дней по следам исчезающего моря", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "От маковых полей Мерке до пещер Каратау — полевой дневник со дна Аральского моря.", "across three regions": "через три региона", "on the road & in camp": "в пути и в лагере", "peak wind on the seabed": "пиковый ветер на дне моря", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "петроглифы в Келиншектау", "The expedition, day by day": "Экспедиция день за днём", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Семь дней, около четырёх тысяч километров, три региона и три климатические зоны — и одно море, что тихо исчезает. Это дневник нашей Аральской экспедиции 2026 года: путь через половину Казахстана, чтобы встать на дно моря, которое некогда было одним из крупнейших озёр на Земле.", "The route · seven chapters": "Маршрут · семь глав", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Алматы → Туркестан", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ озеро Камыстыбас", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Барсакельмес", "→ Kulandy": "→ Куланды", "→ Aralsk": "→ Аральск", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Келиншектау", "→ Almaty": "→ Алматы", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 км · 10 часов в пути", "Almaty": "Алматы", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Маковые поля, Мерке", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Тараз · Жуалынская долина", "Shymkent": "Шымкент", "Turkestan": "Туркестан", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Мы выехали из Алматы в семь утра. Впереди лежали 850 километров до Туркестана — первый длинный перегон через полстраны. По пути остановились у маковых полей близ Мерке: волны красного до самого горизонта, короткая фотосессия — и снова в дорогу.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Плотный обед на объездной Тараза, затем через живописную Жуалынскую долину, где за каждым поворотом одна за другой разворачиваются зелёные холмы. Через Шымкент мы вышли на финальный отрезок.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Десять часов за рулём — и вот он, Туркестан. Город встретил нас неожиданно: перекрытые улицы, полиция повсюду, кортежи. На следующий день готовился саммит глав тюркских государств. Мы нашли свою гостиницу и завели будильник на ранний час — нужно было уехать прежде, чем город перекроют полностью.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Ночёвка: гостиница в Туркестане", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "День первый — маковые поля у Мерке и долгая дорога на юг до Туркестана.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Туркестан → озеро Камыстыбас", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 км · в дельту Сырдарьи", "Kyzylorda": "Кызылорда", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Мемориал Коркыт Ата", "Baikonur viewpoint": "Смотровая площадка Байконур", "Lake Kamystybas": "Озеро Камыстыбас", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Ранний подъём. Нужно было выскользнуть из Туркестана прежде, чем прибудут высокие гости и город закроют окончательно. Завтрак перехватили где-то на трассе. Через Кызылорду — обед, полный бак — и дальше на север.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "Попутный ветер 20 м/с подгонял нас. Как оказалось, ветер станет постоянным спутником всей экспедиции.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Мы задержались у мемориального комплекса Коркыт Ата — благодаря ветру было слышно, как сама степь поёт, когда воздух проходит сквозь древние сооружения. Ещё одна остановка напротив Байконура ради пары снимков с Центром управления полётами на заднем плане.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Уже более чем в 1300 километрах от Алматы мы добрались до озера Камыстыбас — начала дельты Сырдарьи. Мягкая вода, необычайные закаты. Лагерь на берегу. Мы открыли купальный сезон, несмотря на холод и шквалистый ветер. Ужин, закат, предвкушение: завтра — дно Аральского моря.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Ночёвка: дикий лагерь на берегу озера Камыстыбас", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "День второй — мемориал Коркыт Ата, Байконур и лагерь на берегу озера Камыстыбас.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "Казахская степь огромна. Проедь её как следует — и найдёшь время услышать самого себя, просто глядя в окно.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Полевой дневник · Арал 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Камыстыбас → Барсакельмес", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "Дно Аральского моря · ветер до 28 м/с", "Kokaral Dam": "Кокаральская плотина", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Дно Арала · вышка", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Остров Барсакельмес", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Завтрак на берегу озера, затем — к Кокаральской плотине. Именно эта плотина спасла северную часть Аральского моря — примерно пятую часть его прежней площади. Информационный щит на месте приводил цифры, и они были ошеломляющими: объёмы потерянной воды, гектары исчезнувшего моря, сам масштаб экологической катастрофы.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Затем мы поехали по бывшему морскому дну. Машины поднимали плотные облака соли и пыли, которые ветер разносил на километры во все стороны. Горизонт со всех сторон. Вода ушла, оставив после себя постапокалиптические пейзажи. Мы остановились у наблюдательной вышки, с которой инспекторы следят за дикой природой и пожарной опасностью.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "По пути к Барсакельмесу нас накрыла солёно-пылевая буря — видимость упала до пятидесяти метров. Концентрация соли в воздухе была такой, что, выйдя на миг из машины, ты чувствовал, как песок хрустит на зубах. Через два часа на горизонте показалась приподнятая суша. Остров Барсакельмес: когда-то заповедник, из которого звери и птицы давно бежали, по мере того как уходила вода.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Ветер 28 м/с. Мы разбили лагерь у кордона заповедника, укрывшись среди заброшенных построек. Южный край острова — отвесные сорокаметровые обрывы; у подножия — старая баржа, наполовину занесённая песком, сквозь её корпус прорастает саксаул. На севере — севшее на мель судно, до которого ещё не добрались охотники за металлоломом. Безмолвный свидетель катастрофы, гордо стоящий посреди пустоши.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "К вечеру ветер смилостивился, подарив нам костёр и телескоп. Барсакельмес лежит вдали от любого жилья — небо здесь идеально чистое, без светового загрязнения. Вселенная звёзд.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Ночёвка: кордон заповедника Барсакельмес", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "День третий — через сухое дно к Барсакельмесу: Кокаральская плотина, обрывы и затонувшее судно.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Ты стоишь в сорока метрах над землёй, а под тобой когда-то плескалось море на глубине двадцати пяти метров. Теперь здесь нет ничего, кроме песка и пыли.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Барсакельмес · день третий", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Барсакельмес → Куланды", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "Самый трудный этап экспедиции", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Западное дно Арала", "Bozoy": "Бозой", "Kulandy village": "село Куланды", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Утро съёмки дикой природы на Барсакельмесе, завтрак — и дальше. Впереди лежал самый изнурительный отрезок всей экспедиции: западная часть высохшего моря. Мы доверились машинам и относительно плотному грунту. Случись что — эвакуация из этих мест была бы почти невозможна.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Мы прошли. Не без поломок и коварного рельефа, но прошли. Выбравшись на твёрдую дорогу, взяли курс на Бозой. По пути стали появляться табуны лошадей и верблюдов — знак, что люди уже недалеко. В Бозое: заправка, обед — и последний рывок до Куланды.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Вечер в ауле: баня, ужин в гостевом доме, закат над степью. Мы научились доить верблюдиц и познакомились с новорождёнными верблюжатами — удивительно трогательными созданиями. Уснули в старом доме, на традиционных корпе. День, за который стоит быть благодарным.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Ночёвка: гостевой дом в селе Куланды", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "День четвёртый — самый трудный отрезок по западному дну и вечер в Куланды.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Куланды → Аральск", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Западный берег · Северный Арал · портовый город", "Kulandy": "Куланды", "Western shore of the Aral": "Западный берег Арала", "Akespe · hot spring": "Акеспе · горячий источник", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Аральск: музей и порт", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Мы простились с хозяевами в Куланды и двинулись на запад — туда, где старый Арал ещё дышит. Погода была скверная: морось, жестокий ветер. Серое небо, переходящее в серый ландшафт.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "Западный берег. Кромка воды отступила на сотни метров. Мы прошли двести метров пешком по мягкой, разбухшей земле, чтобы добраться до кромки воды. У берега — густая пена соли. Море настолько солёное, что здесь не выживает даже рачок-артемия. Всего три года назад фламинго останавливались тут на пролёте и кормились как раз этими рачками. Теперь вода стала безжизненной.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Мы поехали дальше, к Северному Аралу — посмотреть, что удалось спасти. Село Акеспе: новые дома, магазины, работающий рыбоперерабатывающий завод. Море дало местным жителям шанс жить дальше. Мы искупались в горячем источнике и двинулись к Аральску.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Когда-то крупнейший порт на Аральском море, Аральск теперь стоит в километрах от воды. Экскурсия по музею, прогулка по старой гавани. Ржавеющие остовы портовых кранов — безмолвное напоминание о времени, когда здесь была глубокая вода и кипел порт. Хозяин гостевого дома рассказал, что в последнее время Аральск посещает всё больше иностранных туристов — и местные нашли в этом новый источник дохода. Отрадная новость.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Ночёвка: гостевой дом в Аральске", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "День пятый — умирающий западный берег, Северный Арал и старый порт Аральска.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "Печальное это дело — видеть, как умирает море. Но так уж оно есть.", "The western shore · day five": "Западный берег · день пятый", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Аральск → Келиншектау", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 км · из пустыни в горы", "Aralsk": "Аральск", "Karatau Mountains": "Горы Каратау", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "Горы Келиншектау", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Мы оставили Аральск позади. Ветер наконец стих — но на смену ему пришла тридцатипятиградусная жара. Курс: горы Каратау. По дороге нас встретили дождь и более прохладный воздух — как раз то, что нужно после пустынной пыли.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Шестьсот километров — и мы оказались среди живописных вершин Келиншектау. Лагерь у подножия скал. Закат без ветра — первый за всю экспедицию. Славный ужин под звёздным шатром: тихий, созерцательный вечер после дней, проведённых на краю катастрофы.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Ночёвка: дикий лагерь в горах Келиншектау", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "День шестой — из пустынного зноя в вершины Келиншектау.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Келиншектау → Алматы", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Петроглифы · пещера Акмешит · финиш", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Петроглифы Келиншектау", "Akmeshit Cave": "Пещера Акмешит", "Almaty — journey complete": "Алматы — путешествие завершено", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "Утро началось со сбора лагеря — и уборки мусора, оставленного беспечными посетителями. Затем настала охота за петроглифами. Совершенно захватывающее занятие: обшаривать скалы в поисках древних рисунков и пытаться разгадать, что изобразил художник тысячи лет назад. Наша охота оказалась удачной — более двадцати петроглифов со сценами охоты, фигурами животных и солярными символами.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Следующая остановка: пещера Акмешит. Её масштаб захватывал дух. Ещё поразительнее были цветущие тутовые деревья на дне пещеры, в полумраке под каменным сводом. Несколько эффектных снимков — и мы взяли курс на Алматы.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "Финальная точка путешествия. Четыре тысячи километров, семь дней, три климатические зоны, одно исчезающее море — и впечатления на всю жизнь.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Путешествие завершено — снова в Алматы", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "День седьмой — петроглифы, пещера Акмешит и дорога домой в Алматы.", "In closing": "В заключение", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Семь дней по следам Аральского моря — от безбрежных маковых полей до покрытых солью берегов, от брошенных судов до живых сёл. Казахстан огромен, и чтобы по-настоящему его почувствовать, нужно просто ехать.", "By the numbers": "В цифрах", "One route, in figures": "Один маршрут в цифрах", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Встаньте на дно моря", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Аральская экспедиция, выстроенная под ваши интересы", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Многодневный переход от Алматы до сухого дна Арала — Барсакельмес, затонувшие суда, Кокаральская плотина и живые сёла Северного Арала. Личный транспорт 4×4, опытные гиды, дикие лагеря и гостевые дома по пути.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Смотреть экспедиции →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Заказать частную экспедицию →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.kk, {"Route": "Маршрут", "Day 01": "01-күн", "Day 02": "02-күн", "Day 03": "03-күн", "Day 04": "04-күн", "Day 05": "05-күн", "Day 06": "06-күн", "Day 07": "07-күн", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Дала күнделігі · Экспедиция есебі · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Жоғалып бара жатқан теңіздің ізімен жеті күн", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Меркенің көкнәр алқаптарынан Қаратау үңгірлеріне дейін — Арал теңізінің түбінен жазылған дала күнделігі.", "across three regions": "үш өңір арқылы", "on the road & in camp": "жолда және лагерьде", "peak wind on the seabed": "теңіз түбіндегі ең қатты жел", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "Келіншектаудағы петроглифтер", "The expedition, day by day": "Экспедиция күннен-күнге", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Жеті күн, шамамен төрт мың шақырым, үш өңір мен үш климаттық белдеу — және үнсіз жоғалып бара жатқан бір теңіз. Бұл — біздің 2026 жылғы Арал экспедициясының күнделігі: бір кездері Жердегі ең үлкен көлдердің бірі болған теңіздің түбіне аяқ басу үшін Қазақстанның жартысын кесіп өткен сапар.", "The route · seven chapters": "Маршрут · жеті тарау", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Алматы → Түркістан", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ Қамыстыбас көлі", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Барсакелмес", "→ Kulandy": "→ Құланды", "→ Aralsk": "→ Арал", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Келіншектау", "→ Almaty": "→ Алматы", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 км · жолда 10 сағат", "Almaty": "Алматы", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Көкнәр алқаптары, Мерке", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Тараз · Жуалы аңғары", "Shymkent": "Шымкент", "Turkestan": "Түркістан", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Біз Алматыдан таңғы жетіде жолға шықтық. Алдымызда Түркістанға дейін 850 шақырым жатты — елдің жартысын кесіп өтетін алғашқы ұзақ жол. Жолшыбай Мерке маңындағы көкнәр алқаптарына аялдадық: көкжиекке дейін созылған қызыл толқындар, қысқа фотосессия — және қайтадан жолға.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Тараздың айналма жолында тоқ түскі ас, содан соң әр бұрылыста жасыл төбелер бірінен соң бірі ашылатын көрікті Жуалы аңғары арқылы. Шымкент арқылы соңғы белеске шықтық.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Он сағат жүргеннен кейін — міне, Түркістан. Қала бізді күтпеген жағдайда қарсы алды: жабылған көшелер, жан-жақта полиция, кортеждер. Ертеңіне түркі мемлекеттері басшыларының саммиті дайындалып жатыр екен. Қонақ үйімізді тауып, оянуды ерте сағатқа қойдық — қала толық жабылғанға дейін кетуіміз керек еді.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Түнеу: Түркістандағы қонақ үй", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "Бірінші күн — Мерке маңындағы көкнәр алқаптары және Түркістанға дейінгі ұзақ оңтүстік жол.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Түркістан → Қамыстыбас көлі", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 км · Сырдария атырауына қарай", "Kyzylorda": "Қызылорда", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Қорқыт Ата кесенесі", "Baikonur viewpoint": "Байқоңыр көрінісі", "Lake Kamystybas": "Қамыстыбас көлі", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Ерте жол. Жоғары лауазымды қонақтар келіп, қала толық жабылғанға дейін Түркістаннан шығып кетуіміз керек еді. Таңғы асты тас жолдың бір жерінен іліп алдық. Қызылорда арқылы — түскі ас, толы бак — әрі қарай солтүстікке.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "20 м/с соққан соңғы жел бізді алға итермеледі. Кейін белгілі болғандай, жел бүкіл экспедицияның тұрақты серігіне айналды.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Қорқыт Ата мемориалдық кешеніне аялдадық — желдің арқасында ауа ежелгі құрылыстардан өткенде даланың өзі ән салғандай естілді. Артқы жағында Ұшуды басқару орталығы көрінетін бірнеше сурет үшін Байқоңырға қарама-қарсы тағы бір аялдама.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Алматыдан 1300 шақырымнан астам жерде Қамыстыбас көліне — Сырдария атырауының басына жеттік. Жұмсақ су, ерекше күн батулар. Жағадағы лагерь. Суық пен қатты желге қарамастан, шомылу маусымын аштық. Кешкі ас, күн батуы, күту: ертең — Арал теңізінің түбі.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Түнеу: Қамыстыбас көлінің жағасындағы дала лагері", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "Екінші күн — Қорқыт Ата кесенесі, Байқоңыр және Қамыстыбас көлінің жағасындағы лагерь.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "Қазақ даласы ұшан-теңіз. Оны лайықты кесіп өтсең, тек терезеден қарап отырып-ақ өзіңді тыңдауға уақыт табасың.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Дала күнделігі · Арал 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Қамыстыбас → Барсакелмес", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "Арал теңізінің түбі · жел 28 м/с дейін", "Kokaral Dam": "Көкарал бөгеті", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Арал түбі · мұнара", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Барсакелмес аралы", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Көл жағасында таңғы ас, содан соң Көкарал бөгетіне қарай. Дәл осы бөгет Арал теңізінің солтүстік бөлігін — бұрынғы ауданының шамамен бестен бірін сақтап қалды. Орындағы ақпараттық тақта сандарды көрсетті, ал олар таңғаларлық еді: жоғалған су көлемі, жоғалған теңіз гектарлары, экологиялық апаттың нағыз ауқымы.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Содан кейін бұрынғы теңіз түбімен жүрдік. Көліктер тұз бен шаңның қалың бұлттарын көтерді, оларды жел шақырымдарға таратып жіберді. Айналаның бәрі көкжиек. Су кетіп, артында апокалипсистен кейінгідей пейзаждар қалдырды. Жабайы табиғат пен өрт қаупін бақылау үшін инспекторлар пайдаланатын бақылау мұнарасына аялдадық.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "Барсакелмеске бара жатқанда бізді тұзды-шаңды дауыл басып қалды — көріну қашықтығы елу метрге дейін төмендеді. Ауадағы тұз концентрациясы сондай қою еді, көліктен бір сәтке шыққаннан кейін тістің арасында құм қытырлағанын сезесің. Екі сағаттан кейін көкжиекте көтеріңкі құрлық пайда болды. Барсакелмес аралы: бір кездері қорық болған, су тартылған сайын одан аң мен құс әлдеқашан кетіп қалған.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Жел 28 м/с. Лагерімізді қорық кордонында, тастанды ғимараттардың арасына паналап тіктік. Аралдың оңтүстік шеті — тік қырық метрлік жарлар; етегінде құмға жартылай көмілген ескі баржа, оның корпусынан сексеуіл өсіп шыққан. Солтүстікте — жағаға қонған кеме, оған металл сынығын іздеушілер әлі жеткен жоқ. Бос дала ортасында мақтанышпен тұрған апаттың үнсіз куәгері.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "Кешке қарай жел рақым етіп, бізге от пен телескоп сыйлады. Барсакелмес кез келген елді мекеннен алыс жатыр — мұндағы аспан мүлдем таза, жарық ластануынан ада. Жұлдыздар әлемі.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Түнеу: Барсакелмес қорығының кордоны", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "Үшінші күн — құрғақ теңіз түбі арқылы Барсакелмеске: Көкарал бөгеті, жарлар және батқан кеме.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Сен жерден қырық метр биіктікте тұрсың, ал астыңда бір кездері теңіз жиырма бес метр тереңдікте шайқалатын. Енді мұнда құм мен шаңнан басқа ештеңе жоқ.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Барсакелмес · үшінші күн", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Барсакелмес → Құланды", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "Экспедицияның ең қиын кезеңі", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Аралдың батыс түбі", "Bozoy": "Бозой", "Kulandy village": "Құланды ауылы", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Барсакелместе жабайы табиғатты түсірген таң, таңғы ас — әрі қарай. Алдымызда бүкіл экспедицияның ең әбігерлі учаскесі жатты: кеуіп қалған теңіздің батыс бөлігі. Біз көліктерге және салыстырмалы түрде қатты топыраққа сендік. Бірдеңе бұзылса, бұл өңірден эвакуация мүмкін емес дерлік еді.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Біз өттік. Техникалық ақаулар мен қиын жер бедерінсіз емес, бірақ өттік. Қатты жолға шыққан соң Бозойға бағыт алдық. Жолшыбай жылқы мен түйе үйірлері көріне бастады — адамдар алыс емес деген белгі. Бозойда: жанармай құю, түскі ас — және Құландыға дейінгі соңғы серпіліс.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Ауылдағы кеш: моншаға түсу, қонақ үйде кешкі ас, дала үстіндегі күн батуы. Біз түйе саууды үйрендік және жаңа туған боталарды көрдік — таңғажайып жылы жүзді жандар. Ескі үйде, дәстүрлі көрпелердің үстінде ұйықтап қалдық. Шүкір айтуға тұрарлық күн.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Түнеу: Құланды ауылындағы қонақ үй", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "Төртінші күн — батыс теңіз түбі арқылы ең қиын кезең және Құландыдағы кеш.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Құланды → Арал", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Батыс жаға · Солтүстік Арал · порт қаласы", "Kulandy": "Құланды", "Western shore of the Aral": "Аралдың батыс жағасы", "Akespe · hot spring": "Ақеспе · ыстық бұлақ", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Арал: мұражай және порт", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Құландыдағы үй иелерімен қоштасып, батысқа — ескі Арал әлі тыныс алып жатқан жерге қарай беттедік. Ауа райы нашар еді: майда жаңбыр, қатты жел. Сұр аспан сұр пейзажға ұласып кетті.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "Батыс жаға. Су шеті жүздеген метрге шегінген. Су жиегіне жету үшін жұмсақ, су сіңген жермен екі жүз метр жаяу жүрдік. Жағада — тұздың қалың көбігі. Теңіз сондай тұзды, мұнда артемия шаяны да тірі қалмайды. Небәрі үш жыл бұрын фламинголар көшу кезінде осында аялдап, сол шаяндармен қоректенетін. Енді су жансыз болып қалды.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Біз әрі қарай Солтүстік Аралға — нені сақтап қалғанын көру үшін жүрдік. Ақеспе ауылы: жаңа үйлер, дүкендер, жұмыс істеп тұрған балық өңдеу зауыты. Теңіз жергілікті халыққа өмірін жалғастыруға мүмкіндік берген. Ыстық бұлаққа түсіп, әрі қарай Аралға қарай аттандық.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Бір кездері Арал теңізіндегі ең үлкен порт болған Арал қаласы енді судан шақырымдарға қашықтықта тұр. Мұражайды аралау, ескі айлақта серуен. Порт крандарының тот басқан қаңқалары мұнда терең су мен қызу порт болған заманды үнсіз еске салады. Қонақ үй иесі соңғы кезде Аралға шетелдік туристер көбірек келе бастағанын айтты — жергіліктілер мұнан жаңа күнкөріс көзін тапқан. Көңіл қуантатын жаңалық.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Түнеу: Аралдағы қонақ үй", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "Бесінші күн — өліп бара жатқан батыс жаға, Солтүстік Арал және Аралдың ескі порты.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "Теңіздің өлгенін көру — мұңды нәрсе. Бірақ тағдыр солай.", "The western shore · day five": "Батыс жаға · бесінші күн", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Арал → Келіншектау", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 км · шөлден тауларға", "Aralsk": "Арал", "Karatau Mountains": "Қаратау таулары", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "Келіншектау таулары", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Аралды артта қалдырдық. Жел ақыры басылды — бірақ оның орнына отыз бес градус ыстық келді. Бағытымыз: Қаратау таулары. Жолда жаңбыр мен салқын ауаны кездестірдік — шөл шаңынан кейін дәл керегі.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Алты жүз шақырым — біз Келіншектаудың көрікті шыңдарының арасында жүрдік. Жартастар етегіндегі лагерь. Желсіз күн батуы — бүкіл экспедициядағы алғашқысы. Жұлдызды күмбездің астында тамаша кешкі ас: апат шегінде өткен күндерден кейінгі тыныш, ойлы кеш.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Түнеу: Келіншектау тауларындағы дала лагері", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "Алтыншы күн — шөл ыстығынан Келіншектау шыңдарына.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Келіншектау → Алматы", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Петроглифтер · Ақмешіт үңгірі · мәре", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Келіншектау петроглифтері", "Akmeshit Cave": "Ақмешіт үңгірі", "Almaty — journey complete": "Алматы — сапар аяқталды", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "Таң лагерьді жинаудан — және салғырт келушілер тастап кеткен қоқысты жинаудан басталды. Содан соң петроглифтерді іздеу басталды. Шынымен баурап алатын іс: жартастардан ежелгі бейнелерді іздеп, суретшінің мыңдаған жыл бұрын нені бейнелегенін ажыратуға тырысу. Іздеуіміз нәтижелі болды — аң аулау көріністерін, жануарлар бейнелерін және күн нышандарын бейнелейтін жиырмадан астам петроглиф.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Келесі аялдама: Ақмешіт үңгірі. Оның ауқымы таңғалдырды. Одан да таңғаларлығы — тас күмбездің астындағы ала көлеңкеде, үңгір түбінде гүлдеген тұт ағаштары еді. Бірнеше әсерлі сурет — және Алматыға бағыт алдық.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "Сапардың соңғы нүктесі. Төрт мың шақырым, жеті күн, үш климаттық белдеу, бір жоғалып бара жатқан теңіз — және өмір бойғы әсер.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Сапар аяқталды — қайтадан Алматыда", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "Жетінші күн — петроглифтер, Ақмешіт үңгірі және Алматыға қайтар жол.", "In closing": "Қорытындылай келе", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Арал теңізінің ізімен жеті күн — ұшы-қиырсыз көкнәр алқаптарынан тұз қаптаған жағаларға дейін, тасталған кемелерден тірі ауылдарға дейін. Қазақстан ұлан-ғайыр, оны шынайы сезіну үшін жай ғана жолға шығу керек.", "By the numbers": "Сандармен", "One route, in figures": "Бір маршрут сандармен", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Теңіз түбіне аяқ басыңыз", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Сіздің қызығушылықтарыңызға бейімделген Арал экспедициясы", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Алматыдан Аралдың құрғақ түбіне дейінгі бірнеше күндік өтпелі сапар — Барсакелмес, батқан кемелер, Көкарал бөгеті және Солтүстік Аралдың тірі ауылдары. Жеке 4×4 көлік, кәсіби гидтер, жол бойындағы дала лагерьлері мен қонақ үйлер.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Экспедицияларды қарау →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Жеке экспедицияға өтінім беру →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.de, {"Route": "Route", "Day 01": "Tag 01", "Day 02": "Tag 02", "Day 03": "Tag 03", "Day 04": "Tag 04", "Day 05": "Tag 05", "Day 06": "Tag 06", "Day 07": "Tag 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Feldtagebuch · Expeditionsbericht · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Sieben Tage auf den Spuren des verschwindenden Meeres", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Von den Mohnfeldern bei Merke bis zu den Höhlen des Karatau — ein Feldtagebuch vom Grund des Aralsees.", "across three regions": "über drei Regionen", "on the road & in camp": "unterwegs & im Camp", "peak wind on the seabed": "Spitzenwind auf dem Meeresgrund", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "Petroglyphen in Kelinschektau", "The expedition, day by day": "Die Expedition, Tag für Tag", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Sieben Tage, rund viertausend Kilometer, drei Regionen und drei Klimazonen — und ein Meer, das still verschwindet. Dies ist das Tagebuch unserer Aral-Expedition 2026: eine Fahrt durch das halbe Land, um auf dem Grund eines Meeres zu stehen, das einst einer der größten Seen der Erde war.", "The route · seven chapters": "Die Route · sieben Kapitel", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Almaty → Turkestan", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ Kamystybas-See", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Barsa-Kelmes", "→ Kulandy": "→ Kulandy", "→ Aralsk": "→ Aralsk", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Kelinschektau", "→ Almaty": "→ Almaty", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 10 Stunden Fahrt", "Almaty": "Almaty", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Mohnfelder, Merke", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Taras · Schualy-Tal", "Shymkent": "Schymkent", "Turkestan": "Turkestan", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Um sieben Uhr morgens brachen wir von Almaty auf. Vor uns lagen 850 Kilometer bis Turkestan — die erste lange Etappe durch das halbe Land. Unterwegs hielten wir an den Mohnfeldern bei Merke: rote Wellen bis zum Horizont, ein kurzes Fotoshooting, und weiter ging es.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Ein kräftiges Mittagessen an der Umgehung von Taras, dann durch das malerische Schualy-Tal, wo sich hinter jeder Kurve grüne Hügel auftun. Über Schymkent erreichten wir die letzte Etappe.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Zehn Stunden Fahrt — und da war es, Turkestan. Die Stadt empfing uns unerwartet: abgesperrte Straßen, überall Polizei, Fahrzeugkolonnen. Für den nächsten Tag wurde ein Gipfeltreffen der Staatsoberhäupter der Turkstaaten vorbereitet. Wir fanden unser Hotel und stellten den Wecker auf die frühen Morgenstunden — wir mussten weg, bevor die Stadt völlig abgeriegelt war.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Übernachtung: Hotel in Turkestan", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "Tag eins — die Mohnfelder bei Merke und die lange Straße südwärts nach Turkestan.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Turkestan → Kamystybas-See", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · ins Syrdarja-Delta", "Kyzylorda": "Kysylorda", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Korkyt-Ata-Mausoleum", "Baikonur viewpoint": "Aussichtspunkt Baikonur", "Lake Kamystybas": "Kamystybas-See", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Ein früher Aufbruch. Wir mussten aus Turkestan heraus, bevor die Würdenträger eintrafen und die Stadt völlig abgeriegelt wurde. Das Frühstück gab es irgendwo an der Fernstraße. Durch Kysylorda — Mittagessen, voller Tank — und weiter nach Norden.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "Ein Rückenwind von 20 m/s trieb uns voran. Wie sich zeigte, sollte der Wind die ganze Expedition über unser ständiger Begleiter sein.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Wir machten Halt am Korkyt-Ata-Gedenkkomplex — dank des Windes konnte man die Steppe selbst singen hören, als die Luft durch die alten Bauten strich. Ein weiterer Halt gegenüber von Baikonur für ein paar Fotos mit dem Kontrollzentrum im Hintergrund.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Schon über 1.300 Kilometer von Almaty entfernt erreichten wir den Kamystybas-See — den Anfang des Syrdarja-Deltas. Weiches Wasser, außergewöhnliche Sonnenuntergänge. Camp am Ufer. Wir eröffneten die Badesaison trotz Kälte und Sturmböen. Abendessen, Sonnenuntergang, Vorfreude: morgen der Grund des Aralsees.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Übernachtung: Wildcamp am Ufer des Kamystybas-Sees", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "Tag zwei — das Korkyt-Ata-Mausoleum, Baikonur und das Camp am Ufer des Kamystybas-Sees.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "Die kasachische Steppe ist weit. Durchquert man sie richtig, findet man die Zeit, sich selbst zu hören — einfach beim Blick aus dem Fenster.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Feldtagebuch · Aral 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "Der Grund des Aralsees · Wind bis 28 m/s", "Kokaral Dam": "Kokaral-Damm", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Aralseegrund · Turm", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Insel Barsa-Kelmes", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Frühstück am Seeufer, dann auf zum Kokaral-Damm. Dieser Damm rettete den nördlichen Teil des Aralsees — etwa ein Fünftel seiner einstigen Fläche. Eine Infotafel vor Ort führte die Zahlen auf, und sie waren erschütternd: verlorene Wassermengen, verschwundene Hektar Meer, das schiere Ausmaß der ökologischen Katastrophe.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Dann fuhren wir über den ehemaligen Meeresgrund. Die Fahrzeuge wirbelten dichte Salz- und Staubwolken auf, die der Wind kilometerweit in alle Richtungen trug. Ringsum nur Horizont. Das Wasser war fort und hinterließ postapokalyptische Landschaften. Wir hielten an einem Wachturm, von dem aus Ranger Wildtiere und Brandgefahr überwachen.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "Auf dem Weg nach Barsa-Kelmes verschluckte uns ein Salz- und Staubsturm — die Sicht sank auf fünfzig Meter. Die Salzkonzentration in der Luft war so hoch, dass man nach einem kurzen Aussteigen den Grus zwischen den Zähnen knirschen spürte. Zwei Stunden später tauchte am Horizont eine erhöhte Landmasse auf. Die Insel Barsa-Kelmes: einst ein Naturschutzgebiet, aus dem Tiere und Vögel längst geflohen waren, als das Wasser sich zurückzog.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Wind mit 28 m/s. Wir schlugen das Lager an der Ranger-Station des Reservats auf, geschützt zwischen verlassenen Gebäuden. Der Südrand der Insel — schroffe vierzig Meter hohe Klippen; am Fuß eine alte, halb im Sand versunkene Barke, durch deren Rumpf Saxaul-Bäume wachsen. Im Norden ein auf Grund gelaufenes Schiff, von Schrottsammlern noch unentdeckt. Ein stummer Zeuge der Katastrophe, stolz inmitten der Ödnis.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "Gegen Abend zeigte der Wind Erbarmen und gönnte uns ein Lagerfeuer und ein Teleskop. Barsa-Kelmes liegt fernab jeder Siedlung — der Himmel ist hier vollkommen klar, frei von Lichtverschmutzung. Ein Universum aus Sternen.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Übernachtung: Ranger-Station des Naturschutzgebiets Barsa-Kelmes", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "Tag drei — über den trockenen Meeresgrund nach Barsa-Kelmes: der Kokaral-Damm, die Klippen und das Schiffswrack.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Du stehst vierzig Meter über dem Boden, und unter dir plätscherte einst das Meer in fünfundzwanzig Metern Tiefe. Jetzt ist da nichts als Sand und Staub.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Barsa-Kelmes · Tag drei", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "Die härteste Etappe der Expedition", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Westlicher Aralseegrund", "Bozoy": "Bosoi", "Kulandy village": "Dorf Kulandy", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Ein Morgen mit Tierfotografie auf Barsa-Kelmes, Frühstück, und dann weiter. Vor uns lag der zermürbendste Abschnitt der ganzen Expedition: der westliche Teil des ausgetrockneten Meeres. Wir vertrauten auf die Fahrzeuge und den verhältnismäßig festen Boden. Ginge etwas schief, wäre eine Bergung aus dieser Gegend nahezu unmöglich.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Wir kamen durch. Nicht ohne mechanische Pannen und kniffliges Gelände, aber wir schafften es. Auf fester Straße nahmen wir Kurs auf Bosoi. Unterwegs tauchten Pferde- und Kamelherden auf — ein Zeichen, dass Menschen nicht weit waren. In Bosoi: tanken, Mittagessen und ein letzter Vorstoß nach Kulandy.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Abend im Aul: eine Banja, Abendessen im Gästehaus, Sonnenuntergang über der Steppe. Wir lernten Kamele zu melken und trafen neugeborene Fohlen — bemerkenswert liebenswerte Geschöpfe. Wir schliefen in einem alten Haus auf traditionellen Korpe-Decken ein. Ein Tag zum Dankbarsein.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Übernachtung: Gästehaus im Dorf Kulandy", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "Tag vier — die härteste Etappe über den westlichen Meeresgrund und der Abend in Kulandy.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Kulandy → Aralsk", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Westufer · Nordaral · die Hafenstadt", "Kulandy": "Kulandy", "Western shore of the Aral": "Westufer des Aral", "Akespe · hot spring": "Akespe · heiße Quelle", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Aralsk: Museum & Hafen", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Wir verabschiedeten uns von unseren Gastgebern in Kulandy und fuhren nach Westen — dorthin, wo der alte Aral noch atmet. Das Wetter war scheußlich: Nieselregen, heftiger Wind. Ein grauer Himmel, der in eine graue Landschaft überging.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "Das Westufer. Die Wasserlinie hatte sich um Hunderte Meter zurückgezogen. Zweihundert Meter gingen wir zu Fuß über weichen, durchnässten Boden bis zum Wasserrand. Am Ufer — ein dicker Schaum aus Salz. Das Meer ist so salzig, dass hier nicht einmal Salinenkrebse überleben. Noch vor drei Jahren rasteten hier Flamingos auf ihrem Zug und fraßen eben jene Krebse. Jetzt ist das Wasser leblos geworden.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Wir fuhren weiter zum Nordaral — um zu sehen, was gerettet worden war. Das Dorf Akespe: neue Häuser, Geschäfte, eine funktionierende Fischfabrik. Das Meer hatte den Einheimischen eine Chance gegeben weiterzumachen. Wir badeten in einer heißen Quelle und fuhren dann weiter nach Aralsk.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Einst der größte Hafen am Aralsee, liegt Aralsk heute kilometerweit vom Wasser entfernt. Ein Rundgang durchs Museum, ein Spaziergang durch den alten Hafen. Die rostenden Gerippe der Hafenkräne mahnen still an eine Zeit, als hier tiefes Wasser und ein blühender Hafen waren. Der Gästehaus-Besitzer erzählte uns, dass in letzter Zeit immer mehr ausländische Touristen nach Aralsk kommen — und die Einheimischen darin eine neue Lebensgrundlage gefunden haben. Erfreuliche Nachrichten.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Übernachtung: Gästehaus in Aralsk", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "Tag fünf — das sterbende Westufer, der Nordaral und der alte Hafen von Aralsk.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "Es ist ein wehmütiger Anblick, ein Meer sterben zu sehen. Doch so ist es nun einmal.", "The western shore · day five": "Das Westufer · Tag fünf", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Aralsk → Kelinschektau", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · von der Wüste in die Berge", "Aralsk": "Aralsk", "Karatau Mountains": "Karatau-Gebirge", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "Kelinschektau-Gebirge", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Wir ließen Aralsk hinter uns. Der Wind hatte sich endlich gelegt, nur um von fünfunddreißig Grad Hitze abgelöst zu werden. Unser Ziel: das Karatau-Gebirge. Unterwegs trafen wir auf Regen und kühlere Luft — genau das, was nach dem Wüstenstaub nötig war.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Sechshundert Kilometer, und wir befanden uns inmitten der malerischen Gipfel von Kelinschektau. Camp am Fuß der Felsen. Ein Sonnenuntergang ohne Wind — der erste der ganzen Expedition. Ein feines Abendessen unter einem Sternenzelt: ein stiller, besinnlicher Abend nach Tagen am Rand der Katastrophe.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Übernachtung: Wildcamp im Kelinschektau-Gebirge", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "Tag sechs — aus der Wüstenhitze in die Gipfel von Kelinschektau.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Kelinschektau → Almaty", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Petroglyphen · Akmeschit-Höhle · das Ziel", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Petroglyphen von Kelinschektau", "Akmeshit Cave": "Akmeschit-Höhle", "Almaty — journey complete": "Almaty — Reise abgeschlossen", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "Der Morgen begann mit dem Abbau des Lagers — und dem Einsammeln des Mülls, den achtlose Besucher zurückgelassen hatten. Dann begann die Jagd nach Petroglyphen. Eine durch und durch fesselnde Beschäftigung: die Felsen nach alten Ritzungen absuchen und zu entschlüsseln versuchen, was ein Künstler vor Tausenden von Jahren darstellte. Unsere Jagd war erfolgreich — über zwanzig Petroglyphen mit Jagdszenen, Tierfiguren und Sonnensymbolen.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Nächster Halt: die Akmeschit-Höhle. Ihre Ausmaße waren atemberaubend. Noch erstaunlicher waren die blühenden Maulbeerbäume auf dem Höhlenboden, im Halbdunkel unter dem steinernen Gewölbe. Ein paar eindrucksvolle Fotos, und wir nahmen Kurs auf Almaty.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "Der letzte Punkt der Reise. Viertausend Kilometer, sieben Tage, drei Klimazonen, ein verschwindendes Meer — und Eindrücke für ein ganzes Leben.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Reise abgeschlossen — zurück in Almaty", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "Tag sieben — Petroglyphen, die Akmeschit-Höhle und der Heimweg nach Almaty.", "In closing": "Zum Abschluss", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Sieben Tage im Sog des Aralsees — von endlosen Mohnfeldern zu salzverkrusteten Ufern, von verlassenen Schiffen zu lebendigen Dörfern. Kasachstan ist riesig, und um es wirklich zu spüren, muss man einfach fahren.", "By the numbers": "In Zahlen", "One route, in figures": "Eine Route in Zahlen", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Stehen Sie auf dem Grund des Meeres", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Eine Aral-Expedition, ganz nach Ihren Interessen gestaltet", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Eine mehrtägige Durchquerung von Almaty bis zum trockenen Grund des Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, die Schiffswracks, der Kokaral-Damm und die lebendigen Dörfer des Nordaral. Privater 4×4-Transport, Fachguides, Wildcamps und Gästehäuser entlang der Strecke.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Expeditionen entdecken →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Private Expedition anfragen →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.fr, {"Route": "Itinéraire", "Day 01": "Jour 01", "Day 02": "Jour 02", "Day 03": "Jour 03", "Day 04": "Jour 04", "Day 05": "Jour 05", "Day 06": "Jour 06", "Day 07": "Jour 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Carnet de terrain · Rapport d'expédition · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Sept jours sur les traces de la mer qui disparaît", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Des champs de pavots de Merke aux grottes du Karatau — un carnet de terrain depuis le lit de la mer d'Aral.", "across three regions": "à travers trois régions", "on the road & in camp": "sur la route et au campement", "peak wind on the seabed": "vent maximal sur le fond marin", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "pétroglyphes à Kelinshektau", "The expedition, day by day": "L'expédition, jour après jour", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Sept jours, environ quatre mille kilomètres, trois régions et trois zones climatiques — et une mer qui disparaît en silence. Voici le carnet de notre expédition Aral 2026 : une traversée de la moitié du Kazakhstan pour se tenir sur le lit d'une mer qui fut jadis l'un des plus grands lacs de la planète.", "The route · seven chapters": "L'itinéraire · sept chapitres", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Almaty → Turkestan", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ lac Kamystybas", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Barsa-Kelmes", "→ Kulandy": "→ Kulandy", "→ Aralsk": "→ Aralsk", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Kelinshektau", "→ Almaty": "→ Almaty", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 10 heures de route", "Almaty": "Almaty", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Champs de pavots, Merke", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Taraz · vallée de Zhualy", "Shymkent": "Chymkent", "Turkestan": "Turkestan", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Nous avons quitté Almaty à sept heures du matin. Devant nous, 850 kilomètres jusqu'à Turkestan — la première longue étape à travers la moitié du pays. En chemin, nous nous sommes arrêtés aux champs de pavots près de Merke : des vagues de rouge jusqu'à l'horizon, une courte séance photo, et de nouveau la route.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Un déjeuner copieux sur la rocade de Taraz, puis la pittoresque vallée de Zhualy, où des collines verdoyantes se déploient l'une après l'autre à chaque virage. En passant par Chymkent, nous avons rejoint la dernière ligne droite.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Dix heures de route — et la voilà, Turkestan. La ville nous a accueillis de façon inattendue : rues barricadées, policiers partout, cortèges. Un sommet des chefs d'État turciques se préparait pour le lendemain. Nous avons trouvé notre hôtel et réglé le réveil au petit matin — il fallait partir avant que la ville ne soit entièrement bouclée.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Nuit : hôtel à Turkestan", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "Jour un — les champs de pavots près de Merke et la longue route vers le sud jusqu'à Turkestan.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Turkestan → lac Kamystybas", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · vers le delta du Syr-Daria", "Kyzylorda": "Kyzylorda", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Mémorial de Korkyt Ata", "Baikonur viewpoint": "point de vue sur Baïkonour", "Lake Kamystybas": "lac Kamystybas", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Départ matinal. Il fallait quitter Turkestan avant l'arrivée des dignitaires et le bouclage total de la ville. Le petit-déjeuner s'est attrapé quelque part sur la grand-route. Par Kyzylorda — déjeuner, plein d'essence — puis cap au nord.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "Un vent arrière de 20 m/s nous poussait. Il s'avéra que le vent deviendrait notre compagnon constant pour toute l'expédition.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Nous nous sommes arrêtés au complexe mémoriel de Korkyt Ata — grâce au vent, on entendait la steppe elle-même chanter tandis que l'air traversait les anciennes structures. Un autre arrêt face à Baïkonour pour quelques photos avec le centre de contrôle en arrière-plan.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Déjà à plus de 1 300 kilomètres d'Almaty, nous sommes arrivés au lac Kamystybas — le début du delta du Syr-Daria. Une eau douce, des couchers de soleil extraordinaires. Campement sur la rive. Nous avons ouvert la saison de baignade malgré le froid et les rafales de tempête. Souper, coucher de soleil, impatience : demain, le lit de la mer d'Aral.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Nuit : campement sauvage sur la rive du lac Kamystybas", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "Jour deux — le mémorial de Korkyt Ata, Baïkonour et le campement sur la rive du lac Kamystybas.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "La steppe kazakhe est immense. Traversez-la comme il faut, et vous trouverez le temps de vous écouter — simplement en regardant par la fenêtre.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Carnet de terrain · Aral 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "Le lit de la mer d'Aral · vents jusqu'à 28 m/s", "Kokaral Dam": "Barrage de Kokaral", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Lit de l'Aral · tour", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Île de Barsa-Kelmes", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Petit-déjeuner au bord du lac, puis départ vers le barrage de Kokaral. C'est ce barrage qui a sauvé la partie nord de la mer d'Aral — environ un cinquième de sa superficie d'autrefois. Un panneau d'information sur place exposait les chiffres, et ils étaient effarants : volumes d'eau perdus, hectares de mer disparus, l'ampleur même de la catastrophe écologique.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Puis nous avons roulé sur l'ancien fond marin. Les véhicules soulevaient d'épais nuages de sel et de poussière, dispersés par le vent sur des kilomètres dans toutes les directions. L'horizon partout. L'eau était partie, laissant derrière elle des paysages post-apocalyptiques. Nous nous sommes arrêtés à une tour d'observation d'où les gardes surveillent la faune et les risques d'incendie.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "En route vers Barsa-Kelmes, une tempête de sel et de poussière nous a engloutis — la visibilité est tombée à cinquante mètres. La concentration de sel dans l'air était si forte qu'après être sorti un instant du véhicule, on sentait le grain crisser entre les dents. Deux heures plus tard, une masse de terre surélevée est apparue à l'horizon. L'île de Barsa-Kelmes : autrefois une réserve naturelle, que les animaux et les oiseaux avaient fuie depuis longtemps à mesure que l'eau se retirait.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Vent à 28 m/s. Nous avons planté le camp à la station des gardes de la réserve, à l'abri parmi des bâtiments abandonnés. Le bord sud de l'île — des falaises abruptes de quarante mètres ; à leur pied, une vieille barge à demi ensevelie dans le sable, des saxaouls poussant à travers sa coque. Au nord, un navire échoué, pas encore atteint par les chasseurs de ferraille. Témoin silencieux de la catastrophe, fièrement dressé au milieu du désert.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "Le soir venu, le vent s'est fait clément, nous offrant un feu de camp et un télescope. Barsa-Kelmes se trouve loin de toute habitation — le ciel y est parfaitement clair, sans pollution lumineuse. Un univers d'étoiles.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Nuit : station des gardes de la réserve naturelle de Barsa-Kelmes", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "Jour trois — à travers le fond marin asséché jusqu'à Barsa-Kelmes : le barrage de Kokaral, les falaises et l'épave.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Vous vous tenez à quarante mètres au-dessus du sol, et sous vos pieds la mer clapotait jadis à vingt-cinq mètres de profondeur. Aujourd'hui, il n'y a plus que du sable et de la poussière.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Barsa-Kelmes · jour trois", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "L'étape la plus difficile de l'expédition", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Fond ouest de la mer d'Aral", "Bozoy": "Bozoy", "Kulandy village": "village de Kulandy", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Une matinée de photographie animalière sur Barsa-Kelmes, le petit-déjeuner, puis en avant. Devant nous, le tronçon le plus éprouvant de toute l'expédition : la partie ouest de la mer asséchée. Nous avons mis notre confiance dans les véhicules et le sol relativement ferme. En cas de problème, une évacuation de ces contrées serait quasi impossible.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Nous sommes passés. Non sans incidents mécaniques ni terrain délicat, mais nous y sommes parvenus. Une fois sur route ferme, nous avons mis le cap sur Bozoy. En chemin, des troupeaux de chevaux et de chameaux sont apparus — signe que les hommes n'étaient pas loin. À Bozoy : plein d'essence, déjeuner, et un dernier effort jusqu'à Kulandy.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Soir dans l'aoul : un banya, le souper à la maison d'hôtes, le coucher de soleil sur la steppe. Nous avons appris à traire les chamelles et rencontré des chamelons nouveau-nés — des créatures remarquablement attachantes. Nous nous sommes endormis dans une vieille maison, sur des korpé traditionnels. Une journée dont on est reconnaissant.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Nuit : maison d'hôtes au village de Kulandy", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "Jour quatre — l'étape la plus dure à travers le fond ouest, et le soir à Kulandy.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Kulandy → Aralsk", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Rive ouest · Aral Nord · la ville portuaire", "Kulandy": "Kulandy", "Western shore of the Aral": "Rive ouest de l'Aral", "Akespe · hot spring": "Akespe · source chaude", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Aralsk : musée et port", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Nous avons fait nos adieux à nos hôtes de Kulandy et mis le cap à l'ouest — là où le vieil Aral respire encore. Le temps était exécrable : bruine, vent violent. Un ciel gris se fondant dans un paysage gris.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "La rive ouest. La ligne d'eau avait reculé de plusieurs centaines de mètres. Nous avons marché deux cents mètres sur un sol mou et détrempé pour atteindre le bord de l'eau. Au rivage — une épaisse écume de sel. La mer est si salée que même les artémies n'y survivent pas. Il y a trois ans à peine, les flamants s'arrêtaient lors de leur migration pour se nourrir de ces mêmes crevettes. Aujourd'hui, l'eau est devenue sans vie.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Nous avons poursuivi vers l'Aral Nord — pour voir ce qui avait été sauvé. Le village d'Akespe : maisons neuves, boutiques, une usine de transformation du poisson en activité. La mer avait donné aux habitants une chance de continuer. Nous nous sommes baignés dans une source chaude, puis avons filé vers Aralsk.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Jadis le plus grand port de la mer d'Aral, Aralsk se trouve aujourd'hui à des kilomètres de l'eau. Une visite du musée, une promenade dans le vieux port. Les carcasses rouillées des grues portuaires rappellent en silence l'époque où il y avait ici de l'eau profonde et un port florissant. Le propriétaire de la maison d'hôtes nous a dit que de plus en plus de touristes étrangers viennent à Aralsk ces derniers temps — et que les habitants y ont trouvé une nouvelle source de revenus. Une nouvelle réjouissante.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Nuit : maison d'hôtes à Aralsk", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "Jour cinq — la rive ouest agonisante, l'Aral Nord et le vieux port d'Aralsk.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "C'est une chose mélancolique que de regarder une mer mourir. Mais c'est ainsi.", "The western shore · day five": "La rive ouest · jour cinq", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Aralsk → Kelinshektau", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · du désert aux montagnes", "Aralsk": "Aralsk", "Karatau Mountains": "monts Karatau", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "monts Kelinshektau", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Nous avons laissé Aralsk derrière nous. Le vent était enfin tombé, pour être remplacé par une chaleur de trente-cinq degrés. Notre cap : les monts Karatau. En chemin, nous avons rencontré la pluie et un air plus frais — exactement ce qu'il fallait après la poussière du désert.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Six cents kilomètres, et nous voilà parmi les sommets pittoresques de Kelinshektau. Campement au pied des rochers. Un coucher de soleil sans vent — le premier de toute l'expédition. Un beau souper sous une voûte d'étoiles : une soirée calme et contemplative après des jours passés au bord de la catastrophe.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Nuit : campement sauvage dans les monts Kelinshektau", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "Jour six — de la chaleur du désert aux sommets de Kelinshektau.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Kelinshektau → Almaty", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Pétroglyphes · grotte d'Akmeshit · l'arrivée", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Pétroglyphes de Kelinshektau", "Akmeshit Cave": "Grotte d'Akmeshit", "Almaty — journey complete": "Almaty — voyage achevé", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "La matinée a commencé par le démontage du camp — et le ramassage des déchets laissés par des visiteurs négligents. Puis vint la chasse aux pétroglyphes. Une quête absolument captivante : scruter les rochers à la recherche de gravures anciennes et tenter de déchiffrer ce qu'un artiste a représenté il y a des milliers d'années. Notre chasse fut fructueuse — plus de vingt pétroglyphes figurant des scènes de chasse, des silhouettes d'animaux et des symboles solaires.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Étape suivante : la grotte d'Akmeshit. Ses dimensions étaient à couper le souffle. Plus étonnants encore, les mûriers en fleur sur le sol de la grotte, dans la pénombre sous la voûte de pierre. Quelques clichés saisissants, et nous avons mis le cap sur Almaty.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "Le point final du voyage. Quatre mille kilomètres, sept jours, trois zones climatiques, une mer qui disparaît — et des impressions pour toute une vie.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Voyage achevé — de retour à Almaty", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "Jour sept — pétroglyphes, grotte d'Akmeshit et la route du retour vers Almaty.", "In closing": "En conclusion", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Sept jours dans le sillage de la mer d'Aral — des champs de pavots sans fin aux rivages encroûtés de sel, des navires abandonnés aux villages bien vivants. Le Kazakhstan est immense, et pour le ressentir vraiment, il suffit de rouler.", "By the numbers": "En chiffres", "One route, in figures": "Un itinéraire en chiffres", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Tenez-vous sur le lit de la mer", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Une expédition Aral, conçue selon vos envies", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Une traversée de plusieurs jours d'Almaty jusqu'au lit asséché de l'Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, les épaves, le barrage de Kokaral et les villages bien vivants de l'Aral Nord. Transport privé en 4×4, guides spécialisés, campements sauvages et maisons d'hôtes tout au long du parcours.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Découvrir les expéditions →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Demander une expédition privée →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.it, {"Route": "Itinerario", "Day 01": "Giorno 01", "Day 02": "Giorno 02", "Day 03": "Giorno 03", "Day 04": "Giorno 04", "Day 05": "Giorno 05", "Day 06": "Giorno 06", "Day 07": "Giorno 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Diario di campo · Resoconto di spedizione · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Sette giorni sulle tracce del mare che scompare", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Dai campi di papaveri di Merke alle grotte del Karatau — un diario di campo dal fondo del Lago d'Aral.", "across three regions": "attraverso tre regioni", "on the road & in camp": "in viaggio e in campo", "peak wind on the seabed": "vento massimo sul fondale", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "petroglifi a Kelinshektau", "The expedition, day by day": "La spedizione, giorno per giorno", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Sette giorni, circa quattromila chilometri, tre regioni e tre zone climatiche — e un mare che scompare in silenzio. Questo è il diario della nostra spedizione all'Aral 2026: un viaggio attraverso metà del Kazakhstan per stare sul fondo di un mare che un tempo era uno dei laghi più grandi della Terra.", "The route · seven chapters": "L'itinerario · sette capitoli", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Almaty → Turkestan", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ Lago Kamystybas", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Barsa-Kelmes", "→ Kulandy": "→ Kulandy", "→ Aralsk": "→ Aralsk", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Kelinshektau", "→ Almaty": "→ Almaty", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 10 ore di viaggio", "Almaty": "Almaty", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Campi di papaveri, Merke", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Taraz · valle di Zhualy", "Shymkent": "Shymkent", "Turkestan": "Turkestan", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Siamo partiti da Almaty alle sette del mattino. Davanti a noi 850 chilometri fino a Turkestan — la prima lunga tappa attraverso metà del Paese. Lungo la strada ci siamo fermati ai campi di papaveri vicino a Merke: onde di rosso fino all'orizzonte, una breve sessione fotografica, e di nuovo in viaggio.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Un pranzo abbondante sulla tangenziale di Taraz, poi attraverso la pittoresca valle di Zhualy, dove colline verdi si succedono una dopo l'altra a ogni curva. Passando per Shymkent, ci siamo immessi nell'ultimo tratto.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Dieci ore di guida — ed eccola, Turkestan. La città ci ha accolti in modo inaspettato: strade transennate, polizia ovunque, cortei. Per il giorno seguente si preparava un vertice dei capi di Stato turcofoni. Abbiamo trovato l'hotel e puntato la sveglia alle ore piccole — dovevamo partire prima che la città venisse chiusa del tutto.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Pernottamento: hotel a Turkestan", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "Giorno uno — i campi di papaveri vicino a Merke e la lunga strada verso sud fino a Turkestan.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Turkestan → Lago Kamystybas", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · nel delta del Syr Darya", "Kyzylorda": "Kyzylorda", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Memoriale di Korkyt Ata", "Baikonur viewpoint": "punto panoramico su Baikonur", "Lake Kamystybas": "Lago Kamystybas", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Partenza all'alba. Dovevamo sgattaiolare fuori da Turkestan prima che arrivassero i dignitari e la città si bloccasse del tutto. La colazione l'abbiamo presa da qualche parte lungo la strada. Attraverso Kyzylorda — pranzo, pieno di carburante — e avanti verso nord.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "Un vento in coda di 20 m/s ci spingeva. Si rivelò che il vento sarebbe diventato un compagno costante per tutta la spedizione.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Ci siamo fermati al complesso memoriale di Korkyt Ata — grazie al vento si poteva sentire la steppa stessa cantare mentre l'aria attraversava le antiche strutture. Un'altra sosta di fronte a Baikonur per qualche foto con il Centro di controllo sullo sfondo.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Già a oltre 1.300 chilometri da Almaty, siamo arrivati al Lago Kamystybas — l'inizio del delta del Syr Darya. Acqua dolce, tramonti straordinari. Campo sulla riva. Abbiamo aperto la stagione balneare nonostante il freddo e le raffiche di tempesta. Cena, tramonto, attesa: domani, il fondo del Lago d'Aral.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Pernottamento: campo libero sulla riva del Lago Kamystybas", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "Giorno due — il memoriale di Korkyt Ata, Baikonur e il campo sulla riva del Lago Kamystybas.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "La steppa kazaka è immensa. Attraversala come si deve e troverai il tempo di ascoltare te stesso — semplicemente guardando fuori dal finestrino.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Diario di campo · Aral 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "Il fondo del Lago d'Aral · venti fino a 28 m/s", "Kokaral Dam": "Diga di Kokaral", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Fondo dell'Aral · torre", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Isola di Barsa-Kelmes", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Colazione in riva al lago, poi via verso la diga di Kokaral. Fu questa diga a salvare la porzione settentrionale del Lago d'Aral — circa un quinto della sua superficie di un tempo. Un pannello informativo sul posto riportava le cifre, ed erano sconcertanti: volumi d'acqua perduti, ettari di mare svaniti, la pura entità della catastrofe ecologica.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Poi abbiamo guidato sull'antico fondale. I veicoli sollevavano dense nubi di sale e polvere, disperse dal vento per chilometri in ogni direzione. Orizzonte tutt'intorno. L'acqua se n'era andata, lasciando dietro di sé paesaggi post-apocalittici. Ci siamo fermati a una torre di osservazione usata dai guardiani per sorvegliare la fauna e il rischio incendi.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "Sulla via per Barsa-Kelmes, una tempesta di sale e polvere ci ha avvolti — la visibilità è scesa a cinquanta metri. La concentrazione di sale nell'aria era così intensa che, dopo essere usciti un attimo dal veicolo, si sentiva la sabbia scricchiolare tra i denti. Due ore dopo, una massa di terra rialzata è apparsa all'orizzonte. L'isola di Barsa-Kelmes: un tempo riserva naturale, da cui animali e uccelli erano fuggiti da tempo man mano che l'acqua si ritirava.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Vento a 28 m/s. Abbiamo montato il campo alla stazione dei ranger della riserva, al riparo tra edifici abbandonati. Il margine meridionale dell'isola — ripide scogliere di quaranta metri; ai piedi, una vecchia chiatta mezza sepolta nella sabbia, con saxaul che crescono attraverso lo scafo. A nord, una nave incagliata, non ancora raggiunta dai cacciatori di rottami. Un testimone silenzioso della catastrofe, fiero in mezzo alla desolazione.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "Verso sera il vento si è fatto clemente, concedendoci un falò e un telescopio. Barsa-Kelmes è lontana da qualsiasi insediamento — qui il cielo è perfettamente limpido, libero dall'inquinamento luminoso. Un universo di stelle.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Pernottamento: stazione dei ranger della Riserva naturale di Barsa-Kelmes", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "Giorno tre — attraverso il fondale asciutto fino a Barsa-Kelmes: la diga di Kokaral, le scogliere e il relitto.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Ti trovi a quaranta metri dal suolo, e sotto di te il mare un tempo lambiva a venticinque metri di profondità. Ora non c'è altro che sabbia e polvere.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Barsa-Kelmes · giorno tre", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "La tappa più dura della spedizione", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Fondo occidentale dell'Aral", "Bozoy": "Bozoy", "Kulandy village": "villaggio di Kulandy", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Una mattinata di fotografia naturalistica a Barsa-Kelmes, colazione, e poi avanti. Davanti a noi il tratto più estenuante dell'intera spedizione: la parte occidentale del mare prosciugato. Abbiamo riposto la nostra fiducia nei mezzi e nel terreno relativamente compatto. Se qualcosa fosse andato storto, l'evacuazione da queste zone sarebbe stata pressoché impossibile.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Ce l'abbiamo fatta. Non senza intoppi meccanici e qualche terreno insidioso, ma ce l'abbiamo fatta. Una volta su strada solida, abbiamo puntato verso Bozoy. Lungo il cammino sono comparse mandrie di cavalli e cammelli — segno che la gente non era lontana. A Bozoy: rifornimento, pranzo e un ultimo sforzo fino a Kulandy.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Sera nell'aul: un banya, cena alla guesthouse, tramonto sulla steppa. Abbiamo imparato a mungere i cammelli e incontrato cuccioli appena nati — creature straordinariamente tenere. Ci siamo addormentati in una vecchia casa, su tradizionali trapunte korpe. Una giornata di cui essere grati.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Pernottamento: guesthouse nel villaggio di Kulandy", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "Giorno quattro — la tappa più dura attraverso il fondale occidentale e la sera a Kulandy.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Kulandy → Aralsk", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Sponda occidentale · Aral del Nord · la città portuale", "Kulandy": "Kulandy", "Western shore of the Aral": "Sponda occidentale dell'Aral", "Akespe · hot spring": "Akespe · sorgente termale", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Aralsk: museo e porto", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Abbiamo salutato i nostri ospiti a Kulandy e ci siamo diretti a ovest — là dove il vecchio Aral respira ancora. Il tempo era pessimo: pioviggine, vento feroce. Un cielo grigio che sfumava in un paesaggio grigio.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "La sponda occidentale. La linea dell'acqua si era ritirata di centinaia di metri. Abbiamo camminato duecento metri a piedi su terreno molle e fradicio per raggiungere il bordo dell'acqua. Sulla riva — una spessa schiuma di sale. Il mare è così salino che qui non sopravvivono nemmeno le artemie. Solo tre anni fa i fenicotteri si fermavano durante la migrazione per nutrirsi proprio di quei gamberetti. Ora l'acqua è diventata priva di vita.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Abbiamo proseguito verso l'Aral del Nord — per vedere ciò che era stato salvato. Il villaggio di Akespe: case nuove, negozi, uno stabilimento ittico in funzione. Il mare aveva dato alla gente del posto la possibilità di andare avanti. Ci siamo immersi in una sorgente termale, poi abbiamo spinto fino ad Aralsk.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Un tempo il più grande porto del Lago d'Aral, Aralsk oggi si trova a chilometri dall'acqua. Una visita al museo, una passeggiata nel vecchio porto. Le carcasse arrugginite delle gru portuali sono un silenzioso promemoria di un tempo in cui qui c'erano acque profonde e un porto fiorente. Il proprietario della guesthouse ci ha raccontato che ultimamente sempre più turisti stranieri visitano Aralsk — e gli abitanti vi hanno trovato una nuova fonte di sostentamento. Una notizia confortante.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Pernottamento: guesthouse ad Aralsk", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "Giorno cinque — la sponda occidentale morente, l'Aral del Nord e il vecchio porto di Aralsk.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "È una cosa malinconica vedere morire un mare. Ma così va.", "The western shore · day five": "La sponda occidentale · giorno cinque", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Aralsk → Kelinshektau", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · dal deserto alle montagne", "Aralsk": "Aralsk", "Karatau Mountains": "Monti Karatau", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "Monti Kelinshektau", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Ci siamo lasciati Aralsk alle spalle. Il vento si era finalmente placato, solo per essere sostituito da un caldo di trentacinque gradi. La nostra meta: i Monti Karatau. Lungo la strada abbiamo incontrato pioggia e aria più fresca — proprio ciò che serviva dopo la polvere del deserto.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Seicento chilometri, e ci siamo ritrovati tra le pittoresche vette di Kelinshektau. Campo ai piedi delle rocce. Un tramonto senza vento — il primo dell'intera spedizione. Una bella cena sotto una volta di stelle: una serata tranquilla e contemplativa dopo giorni trascorsi sull'orlo della catastrofe.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Pernottamento: campo libero nei Monti Kelinshektau", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "Giorno sei — dal caldo del deserto alle vette di Kelinshektau.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Kelinshektau → Almaty", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Petroglifi · Grotta di Akmeshit · l'arrivo", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Petroglifi di Kelinshektau", "Akmeshit Cave": "Grotta di Akmeshit", "Almaty — journey complete": "Almaty — viaggio concluso", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "La mattina è iniziata smontando il campo — e raccogliendo i rifiuti lasciati da visitatori incuranti. Poi è arrivata la caccia ai petroglifi. Un'attività del tutto avvincente: perlustrare le rocce in cerca di antiche incisioni e cercare di decifrare ciò che un artista raffigurò migliaia di anni fa. La nostra caccia si è rivelata fruttuosa — oltre venti petroglifi con scene di caccia, figure di animali e simboli solari.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Tappa successiva: la Grotta di Akmeshit. Le dimensioni erano mozzafiato. Ancora più sorprendenti erano i gelsi in fiore sul fondo della grotta, nella penombra sotto la volta di pietra. Qualche scatto suggestivo, e abbiamo puntato verso Almaty.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "Il punto finale del viaggio. Quattromila chilometri, sette giorni, tre zone climatiche, un mare che scompare — e impressioni per tutta la vita.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Viaggio concluso — di nuovo ad Almaty", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "Giorno sette — petroglifi, Grotta di Akmeshit e la strada di casa verso Almaty.", "In closing": "Per concludere", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Sette giorni sulla scia del Lago d'Aral — da sconfinati campi di papaveri a rive incrostate di sale, da navi abbandonate a villaggi vivi. Il Kazakhstan è immenso, e per sentirlo davvero basta mettersi in viaggio.", "By the numbers": "In cifre", "One route, in figures": "Un itinerario in cifre", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Sta' sul fondo del mare", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Una spedizione all'Aral, costruita sui tuoi interessi", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Una traversata di più giorni da Almaty al fondo asciutto dell'Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, i relitti, la diga di Kokaral e i villaggi vivi dell'Aral del Nord. Trasporto privato 4×4, guide specializzate, campi liberi e guesthouse lungo il percorso.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Esplora le spedizioni →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Richiedi una spedizione privata →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.zh, {"Route": "路线", "Day 01": "第01天", "Day 02": "第02天", "Day 03": "第03天", "Day 04": "第04天", "Day 05": "第05天", "Day 06": "第06天", "Day 07": "第07天", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "野外日志 · 考察报告 · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "七天追寻正在消失的海", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "从梅尔克的罂粟花田到卡拉套的洞穴——一份来自咸海海床的野外日志。", "across three regions": "横跨三个州", "on the road & in camp": "在路上与营地", "peak wind on the seabed": "海床上的最大风速", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "克林舍克套的岩画", "The expedition, day by day": "考察，逐日记录", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "七天，约四千公里，三个州、三个气候带——以及一片正在悄然消失的海。这是我们2026年咸海考察的日志：驱车穿越半个哈萨克斯坦，只为站在这片曾是地球上最大湖泊之一的海床上。", "The route · seven chapters": "路线 · 七个篇章", "Almaty → Turkestan": "阿拉木图 → 突厥斯坦", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ 卡梅斯特巴斯湖", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ 巴尔萨克尔梅斯", "→ Kulandy": "→ 库兰德", "→ Aralsk": "→ 阿拉尔斯克", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ 克林舍克套", "→ Almaty": "→ 阿拉木图", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 公里 · 在路上 10 小时", "Almaty": "阿拉木图", "Poppy fields, Merke": "罂粟花田，梅尔克", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "塔拉兹 · 茹阿雷河谷", "Shymkent": "奇姆肯特", "Turkestan": "突厥斯坦", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "我们清晨七点从阿拉木图出发。前方是通往突厥斯坦的850公里——穿越半个国家的第一段长途。途中，我们在梅尔克附近的罂粟花田停留：一片片红色绵延至地平线，快速拍了些照片，便又上路。", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "在塔拉兹绕城路上饱餐一顿，随后穿过风景如画的茹阿雷河谷，每一个弯道后，绿色的山丘接连展开。经过奇姆肯特，我们进入最后一段路程。", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "驱车十小时——突厥斯坦终于到了。这座城市以意想不到的方式迎接我们：街道被封锁，警察随处可见，车队来往。次日将举行突厥国家元首峰会。我们找到酒店，把闹钟定在凌晨——必须在全城彻底封锁之前离开。", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "住宿：突厥斯坦的酒店", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "第一天——梅尔克附近的罂粟花田，以及南下突厥斯坦的漫漫长路。", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "突厥斯坦 → 卡梅斯特巴斯湖", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 公里 · 进入锡尔河三角洲", "Kyzylorda": "克孜勒奥尔达", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "科尔库特·阿塔纪念陵", "Baikonur viewpoint": "拜科努尔观景点", "Lake Kamystybas": "卡梅斯特巴斯湖", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "早早出发。我们得在要员抵达、全城封锁之前溜出突厥斯坦。早餐在公路边某处匆匆解决。经过克孜勒奥尔达——午餐、加满油——继续北行。", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "20米/秒的顺风推着我们前行。后来证明，风将成为整个考察过程中始终相伴的伙伴。", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "我们在科尔库特·阿塔纪念建筑群停留——多亏了风，当空气穿过古老的建筑时，你能听见草原本身在歌唱。又在拜科努尔对面停了一站，以飞行控制中心为背景拍了几张照片。", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "已离阿拉木图1300多公里，我们抵达卡梅斯特巴斯湖——锡尔河三角洲的起点。柔软的湖水，非凡的日落。在岸边扎营。尽管寒冷且狂风大作，我们仍开启了游泳季。晚餐、日落、期待：明天，便是咸海的海床。", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "住宿：卡梅斯特巴斯湖畔野营", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "第二天——科尔库特·阿塔纪念陵、拜科努尔，以及卡梅斯特巴斯湖畔的营地。", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "哈萨克草原辽阔无垠。好好地穿行其间，你便会找到聆听自己内心的时间——只需望向窗外。", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "野外日志 · 咸海 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "卡梅斯特巴斯 → 巴尔萨克尔梅斯", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "咸海海床 · 风速达28米/秒", "Kokaral Dam": "科卡拉尔大坝", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "咸海海床 · 瞭望塔", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "巴尔萨克尔梅斯岛", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "在湖畔用过早餐，便前往科卡拉尔大坝。正是这座大坝拯救了咸海的北部——约为其昔日面积的五分之一。现场的信息牌列出了数据，触目惊心：失去的水量、消失的海域公顷数，以及这场生态灾难的庞大规模。", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "随后我们驶过昔日的海床。车辆扬起浓密的盐尘，被风吹散到四面八方数公里之外。四周皆是地平线。水已退去，留下末世般的景象。我们在一座瞭望塔停下，护林员便是从这里监测野生动物与火灾隐患。", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "前往巴尔萨克尔梅斯的途中，一场盐尘暴将我们吞没——能见度降至五十米。空气中的盐分浓度极高，下车片刻，就能感到牙缝间砂砾在咯吱作响。两小时后，地平线上出现一片隆起的陆地。巴尔萨克尔梅斯岛：曾是一处自然保护区，随着水位退去，动物与鸟类早已逃离。", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "风速28米/秒。我们在保护区护林站扎营，躲进废弃的建筑之间。岛的南缘——是四十米高的陡峭悬崖；崖脚下，一艘半埋在沙中的旧驳船，梭梭树从船体中长出。北面，一艘搁浅的船，拾荒者尚未触及。它是这场灾难沉默的见证者，傲然矗立在荒原之中。", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "入夜时分，风终于发了慈悲，让我们得以生起篝火、架起望远镜。巴尔萨克尔梅斯远离任何聚居地——这里的天空澄澈无比，没有光污染。漫天繁星，宛如整个宇宙。", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "住宿：巴尔萨克尔梅斯自然保护区护林站", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "第三天——穿越干涸的海床前往巴尔萨克尔梅斯：科卡拉尔大坝、悬崖与沉船。", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "你站在离地四十米的高处，而在你脚下，海水曾在二十五米深处拍打。如今，只剩下沙与尘。", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "巴尔萨克尔梅斯 · 第三天", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "巴尔萨克尔梅斯 → 库兰德", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "考察中最艰难的一段", "Western Aral Sea bed": "咸海西部海床", "Bozoy": "博佐伊", "Kulandy village": "库兰德村", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "在巴尔萨克尔梅斯拍摄野生动物的一个上午，用过早餐，便继续前行。前方是整个考察中最磨人的一段：干涸海域的西部。我们把希望寄托在车辆和相对坚实的地面上。一旦出事，要从这一带撤离几乎是不可能的。", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "我们闯了过去。虽不免有机械故障和棘手的路况，但终究过来了。一上坚实的公路，便朝博佐伊进发。沿途，成群的马匹与骆驼出现了——意味着人烟已不再遥远。在博佐伊：加油、午餐，再做最后一程冲刺，直奔库兰德。", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "村中的夜晚：洗一次蒸汽浴，在民宿用晚餐，看草原上的落日。我们学会了挤骆驼奶，还见到了刚出生的幼驼——格外惹人怜爱的小生灵。我们在一座老屋里、铺着传统的科尔佩花褥上入睡。值得感恩的一天。", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "住宿：库兰德村的民宿", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "第四天——穿越西部海床最艰难的一段，以及库兰德的夜晚。", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "库兰德 → 阿拉尔斯克", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "西岸 · 北咸海 · 港口小镇", "Kulandy": "库兰德", "Western shore of the Aral": "咸海西岸", "Akespe · hot spring": "阿克斯佩 · 温泉", "Aralsk: museum & port": "阿拉尔斯克：博物馆与港口", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "我们告别了库兰德的主人，向西进发——前往老咸海仍在喘息的地方。天气恶劣：细雨，狂风。灰色的天空融入灰色的大地。", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "西岸。水线已退去数百米。我们徒步走过两百米松软泥泞的地面，才抵达水边。岸边，是一层厚厚的盐沫。海水咸到连卤虫都无法存活。就在三年前，火烈鸟还会在迁徙途中停下，以这些卤虫为食。如今，水已了无生机。", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "我们继续驶向北咸海——去看看被保住的部分。阿克斯佩村：新建的房屋、商店，还有一家运转中的鱼类加工厂。海给了当地人继续生活下去的机会。我们在温泉里泡了泡，便赶往阿拉尔斯克。", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "阿拉尔斯克曾是咸海最大的港口，如今却离水有数公里之遥。参观博物馆，漫步旧港。锈蚀的港口起重机残骸，无声地提醒着这里曾有深水与繁忙港口的岁月。民宿主人告诉我们，近来越来越多的外国游客来到阿拉尔斯克——当地人也由此找到了新的生计。令人欣慰的消息。", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "住宿：阿拉尔斯克的民宿", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "第五天——垂死的西岸、北咸海，以及阿拉尔斯克的旧港。", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "眼看着一片海死去，是件令人黯然的事。可世事本就如此。", "The western shore · day five": "西岸 · 第五天", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "阿拉尔斯克 → 克林舍克套", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 公里 · 从沙漠到群山", "Aralsk": "阿拉尔斯克", "Karatau Mountains": "卡拉套山", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "克林舍克套山", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "我们把阿拉尔斯克抛在身后。风终于停了，取而代之的却是三十五度的酷热。我们的方向：卡拉套山。途中遇上了雨和清凉的空气——这正是在沙漠尘土之后所需要的。", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "六百公里之后，我们置身于克林舍克套秀美的群峰之间。在岩石脚下扎营。一场无风的日落——整个考察中的头一回。在繁星穹顶下享用一顿美餐：在灾难边缘度过数日之后，这是一个宁静而沉思的夜晚。", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "住宿：克林舍克套山中野营", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "第六天——从沙漠的酷热走进克林舍克套的群峰。", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "克林舍克套 → 阿拉木图", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "岩画 · 阿克梅希特洞 · 终点", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "克林舍克套岩画", "Akmeshit Cave": "阿克梅希特洞", "Almaty — journey complete": "阿拉木图——旅程结束", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "清晨从拔营开始——还顺手捡走了粗心游客留下的垃圾。接着便是寻找岩画。这是一件极其引人入胜的事：在岩石间细细搜寻古老的刻画，试图辨认数千年前的艺术家究竟描绘了什么。我们的搜寻收获颇丰——二十余幅岩画，描绘着狩猎场景、动物形象与太阳符号。", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "下一站：阿克梅希特洞。其规模令人叹为观止。更令人惊奇的，是洞底那些盛开的桑树，在石穹之下的微光中静静绽放。拍了几张震撼的照片，我们便朝阿拉木图驶去。", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "旅程的终点。四千公里，七天，三个气候带，一片正在消失的海——以及一生难忘的印象。", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "旅程结束——重回阿拉木图", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "第七天——岩画、阿克梅希特洞，以及回阿拉木图的归途。", "In closing": "结语", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "追随咸海的七天——从无边的罂粟花田到盐壳覆盖的海岸，从废弃的船只到充满生气的村庄。哈萨克斯坦辽阔无垠，要真正感受它，你只需驱车上路。", "By the numbers": "数字一览", "One route, in figures": "一条路线，用数字说话", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "站上这片海的海床", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "一次围绕您兴趣量身定制的咸海考察", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "一段从阿拉木图到咸海干涸海床的多日穿越——巴尔萨克尔梅斯、沉船、科卡拉尔大坝，以及北咸海充满生气的村庄。专属4×4越野车、专业向导，沿途野营与民宿。", "Explore Expeditions →": "探索考察行程 →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "申请私人考察 →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.ja, {"Route": "ルート", "Day 01": "1日目", "Day 02": "2日目", "Day 03": "3日目", "Day 04": "4日目", "Day 05": "5日目", "Day 06": "6日目", "Day 07": "7日目", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "フィールドジャーナル · 遠征レポート · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "消えゆく海をたどる七日間", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "メルケのケシ畑からカラタウの洞窟まで——アラル海の海底からのフィールドジャーナル。", "across three regions": "三つの州にまたがって", "on the road & in camp": "道中とキャンプにて", "peak wind on the seabed": "海底での最大風速", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "ケリンシェクタウの岩絵", "The expedition, day by day": "遠征、その日々の記録", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "七日間、約四千キロ、三つの州と三つの気候帯——そして静かに消えゆく一つの海。これは私たちの2026年アラル遠征の記録です。かつて地球最大級の湖だった海の海底に立つため、カザフスタンの半分を車で横断した旅。", "The route · seven chapters": "ルート · 七つの章", "Almaty → Turkestan": "アルマトイ → トルキスタン", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ カムストゥバス湖", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ バルサケルメス", "→ Kulandy": "→ クランドゥ", "→ Aralsk": "→ アラリスク", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ ケリンシェクタウ", "→ Almaty": "→ アルマトイ", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 走行10時間", "Almaty": "アルマトイ", "Poppy fields, Merke": "ケシ畑、メルケ", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "タラズ · ジュアル渓谷", "Shymkent": "シムケント", "Turkestan": "トルキスタン", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "私たちは朝七時にアルマトイを出発した。前方にはトルキスタンまでの850キロ——国の半分を横断する最初の長距離区間が待っていた。途中、メルケ近郊のケシ畑に立ち寄った。地平線まで続く赤の波、手早い撮影、そして再び道へ。", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "タラズのバイパスでたっぷりの昼食をとり、続いて絵のように美しいジュアル渓谷へ。カーブを曲がるたびに緑の丘が次々と広がる。シムケントを抜け、最後の行程に入った。", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "十時間の運転——そしてトルキスタンが現れた。街は思いがけない様子で私たちを迎えた。封鎖された通り、至る所に警察、車列。翌日にはテュルク諸国首脳会議が準備されていた。私たちはホテルを見つけ、目覚ましを未明にセットした——街が完全に封鎖される前に出発しなければならなかった。", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "宿泊：トルキスタンのホテル", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "一日目——メルケ近郊のケシ畑と、トルキスタンへの長い南下路。", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "トルキスタン → カムストゥバス湖", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · シルダリヤ・デルタへ", "Kyzylorda": "クズロルダ", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "コルクト・アタ廟", "Baikonur viewpoint": "バイコヌール展望地", "Lake Kamystybas": "カムストゥバス湖", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "早朝の出発。要人が到着し街が完全封鎖される前に、トルキスタンを抜け出さねばならなかった。朝食は幹線道路のどこかで手早く済ませた。クズロルダを抜け——昼食、満タン——さらに北へ。", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "毎秒20メートルの追い風が私たちを押し進めた。後にわかったことだが、風は遠征の全行程を通じて絶え間ない同行者となった。", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "コルクト・アタ廟の記念建築群に立ち寄った——風のおかげで、古い構造物を空気が抜けるとき、草原そのものが歌うのが聞こえた。バイコヌールの対岸でもう一度停まり、飛行管制センターを背景に数枚の写真を撮った。", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "アルマトイからすでに1300キロ以上、私たちはカムストゥバス湖——シルダリヤ・デルタの始まり——に着いた。柔らかな水、並外れた夕焼け。岸辺でキャンプ。寒さと暴風のような突風にもかかわらず、私たちは遊泳シーズンの幕を開けた。夕食、日没、そして期待——明日はアラル海の海底だ。", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "宿泊：カムストゥバス湖畔の野営", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "二日目——コルクト・アタ廟、バイコヌール、そしてカムストゥバス湖畔のキャンプ。", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "カザフの草原は果てしなく広い。きちんと走り抜ければ、ただ窓の外を眺めるだけで、自分自身の声を聞く時間が見つかる。", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "フィールドジャーナル · アラル 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "カムストゥバス → バルサケルメス", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "アラル海の海底 · 風速28m/sまで", "Kokaral Dam": "コカラル堤防", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "アラル海底 · 監視塔", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "バルサケルメス島", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "湖畔で朝食をとり、コカラル堤防へ向かった。アラル海の北部——かつての面積のおよそ五分の一——を救ったのは、この堤防だった。現地の案内板に並ぶ数字は、衝撃的だった。失われた水量、消えた海のヘクタール、そして生態系破壊の途方もない規模。", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "それから私たちはかつての海底を走り抜けた。車は塩と砂塵の濃い雲を巻き上げ、風がそれを四方へ何キロも吹き散らした。周囲はどこまでも地平線。水は去り、終末後のような風景を残していた。野生動物と火災の危険を監視員が見張る監視塔で、私たちは足を止めた。", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "バルサケルメスへ向かう途中、塩と砂塵の嵐に呑み込まれた——視界は五十メートルまで落ちた。空気中の塩分濃度はあまりに高く、ほんの一瞬車を降りただけで、歯の間で砂利がきしむのを感じた。二時間後、地平線に隆起した陸地が現れた。バルサケルメス島——かつての自然保護区。水が退くにつれ、動物や鳥はとうに逃げ去っていた。", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "風速28メートル。私たちは保護区の監視所にキャンプを張り、廃墟と化した建物の間に身を寄せた。島の南端——四十メートルの切り立った崖。その麓には、砂に半ば埋もれた古い艀があり、船体を貫いてサクサウルが生えていた。北には座礁した船——まだ金属くず漁りの手は及んでいない。荒野のただ中に誇らしげに立つ、惨事の沈黙の証人だ。", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "夕方になると、風は慈悲を見せ、焚き火と望遠鏡を私たちに許してくれた。バルサケルメスはどんな集落からも遠く離れている——ここの空は完璧に澄み、光害がない。星々の宇宙だ。", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "宿泊：バルサケルメス自然保護区の監視所", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "三日目——乾いた海底を越えてバルサケルメスへ。コカラル堤防、崖、そして難破船。", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "あなたは地上四十メートルの高さに立っている。その足下では、かつて海が二十五メートルの深さで打ち寄せていた。今はもう、砂と塵のほかには何もない。", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "バルサケルメス · 三日目", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "バルサケルメス → クランドゥ", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "遠征で最も過酷な行程", "Western Aral Sea bed": "アラル海西部の海底", "Bozoy": "ボゾイ", "Kulandy village": "クランドゥ村", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "バルサケルメスで野生動物を撮影する朝、朝食、そして出発。前方には遠征全体で最も過酷な区間——干上がった海の西部が待っていた。私たちは車両と、比較的締まった地面に望みを託した。万一何かあれば、この地からの脱出はほぼ不可能だっただろう。", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "私たちは突破した。機械の不調や厄介な地形がなかったわけではないが、やり遂げた。固い道に出ると、ボゾイへ針路を取った。途中、馬とラクダの群れが現れた——人里が遠くない印だ。ボゾイでは給油、昼食、そしてクランドゥへの最後のひと押し。", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "村の夕べ——バーニャ(蒸し風呂)、ゲストハウスでの夕食、草原に沈む夕日。私たちはラクダの乳搾りを習い、生まれたばかりの仔ラクダに出会った——驚くほど愛らしい生き物だ。古い家で、伝統的なコルペの布団に横たわり眠りについた。感謝すべき一日だった。", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "宿泊：クランドゥ村のゲストハウス", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "四日目——西部の海底を越える最も過酷な行程、そしてクランドゥの夕べ。", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "クランドゥ → アラリスク", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "西岸 · 北アラル · 港町", "Kulandy": "クランドゥ", "Western shore of the Aral": "アラルの西岸", "Akespe · hot spring": "アケスペ · 温泉", "Aralsk: museum & port": "アラリスク：博物館と港", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "クランドゥの主人たちに別れを告げ、西へ向かった——古いアラルがまだ息づく場所へ。天気はひどかった。霧雨、激しい風。灰色の空が灰色の風景へと溶け込んでいった。", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "西岸。水際は数百メートルも後退していた。私たちは柔らかくぬかるんだ地面を二百メートル歩いて、ようやく水際にたどり着いた。岸辺には、塩の分厚い泡。海はあまりに塩辛く、アルテミアさえここでは生きられない。ほんの三年前まで、フラミンゴが渡りの途中に立ち寄り、まさにそのアルテミアを食べていた。今や水は生命を失ってしまった。", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "私たちは北アラルへと車を進めた——何が救われたのかを見るために。アケスペ村——新しい家々、商店、稼働する魚加工場。海は地元の人々に、生き続ける機会を与えていた。温泉に浸かり、それからアラリスクへと急いだ。", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "かつてアラル海最大の港だったアラリスクは、今や水から何キロも離れて立っている。博物館を巡り、古い港を歩いた。錆びついた港湾クレーンの残骸が、かつてここに深い水と栄えた港があった時代を、静かに思い起こさせる。ゲストハウスの主人は、近ごろアラリスクを訪れる外国人観光客が増えていると語った——地元の人々はそこに新たな生計の糧を見出したのだ。心温まる知らせだった。", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "宿泊：アラリスクのゲストハウス", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "五日目——死にゆく西岸、北アラル、そしてアラリスクの古い港。", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "海が死んでいくのを見るのは、もの悲しいことだ。だが、それもまた世の習い。", "The western shore · day five": "西岸 · 五日目", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "アラリスク → ケリンシェクタウ", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · 砂漠から山々へ", "Aralsk": "アラリスク", "Karatau Mountains": "カラタウ山脈", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "ケリンシェクタウ山脈", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "私たちはアラリスクを後にした。風はようやく収まったが、代わりに三十五度の暑さがやってきた。目指すはカラタウ山脈。道中で雨と涼しい空気に出会った——砂漠の砂塵のあとには、まさに必要なものだった。", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "六百キロを経て、私たちはケリンシェクタウの美しい峰々の間にいた。岩の麓でキャンプ。風のない夕焼け——遠征全体で初めてのことだった。満天の星空の下での上等な夕食。惨事の縁で過ごした日々のあとの、静かで思索的な夜だった。", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "宿泊：ケリンシェクタウ山中の野営", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "六日目——砂漠の暑さから、ケリンシェクタウの峰々へ。", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "ケリンシェクタウ → アルマトイ", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "岩絵 · アクメシト洞窟 · ゴール", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "ケリンシェクタウの岩絵", "Akmeshit Cave": "アクメシト洞窟", "Almaty — journey complete": "アルマトイ——旅の完結", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "朝は撤営から始まった——そして、心ない訪問者が残したゴミを拾い集めることも。それから岩絵探しが始まった。実に夢中になる営みだ。岩を隈なく探して古代の刻線を見つけ、数千年前の絵師が何を描いたのかを読み解こうとする。私たちの探索は実を結んだ——狩猟の場面、動物の姿、太陽の象徴を描いた二十を超える岩絵。", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "次の目的地はアクメシト洞窟。その規模は息を呑むほどだった。さらに驚かされたのは、石の天蓋の下の薄明かりの中、洞窟の床で花を咲かせる桑の木々だった。印象的な写真を数枚撮り、私たちはアルマトイへ針路を定めた。", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "旅の最終地点。四千キロ、七日間、三つの気候帯、消えゆく一つの海——そして一生分の感動。", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "旅の完結——アルマトイへ帰還", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "七日目——岩絵、アクメシト洞窟、そしてアルマトイへの帰路。", "In closing": "おわりに", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "アラル海の跡をたどる七日間——果てしないケシ畑から塩に覆われた岸辺へ、打ち捨てられた船から生き生きとした村々へ。カザフスタンは広大で、それを本当に感じるには、ただ車を走らせるしかない。", "By the numbers": "数字で見る", "One route, in figures": "ひとつのルートを数字で", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "海の底に立つ", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "あなたの興味に合わせて設計するアラル遠征", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "アルマトイからアラルの乾いた海底までの数日間の縦断——バルサケルメス、難破船、コカラル堤防、そして北アラルの生き生きとした村々。専用の4×4車両、専門ガイド、道中の野営とゲストハウス。", "Explore Expeditions →": "遠征を見る →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "プライベート遠征を申し込む →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.ko, {"Route": "경로", "Day 01": "1일차", "Day 02": "2일차", "Day 03": "3일차", "Day 04": "4일차", "Day 05": "5일차", "Day 06": "6일차", "Day 07": "7일차", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "현장 일지 · 탐험 보고서 · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "사라져 가는 바다를 좇은 7일", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "메르케의 양귀비 들판에서 카라타우의 동굴까지 — 아랄해 바닥에서 적은 현장 일지.", "across three regions": "세 개 주를 가로질러", "on the road & in camp": "길 위에서 그리고 야영지에서", "peak wind on the seabed": "해저에서의 최대 풍속", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "켈린셱타우의 암각화", "The expedition, day by day": "탐험, 하루하루", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "7일, 약 4천 킬로미터, 세 개의 주와 세 개의 기후대 — 그리고 조용히 사라져 가는 하나의 바다. 이것은 2026년 우리 아랄 탐험의 일지입니다. 한때 지구에서 가장 큰 호수 중 하나였던 바다의 바닥에 서기 위해 카자흐스탄의 절반을 가로지른 여정.", "The route · seven chapters": "경로 · 일곱 장", "Almaty → Turkestan": "알마티 → 투르키스탄", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ 카미스티바스 호수", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ 바르사켈메스", "→ Kulandy": "→ 쿨란디", "→ Aralsk": "→ 아랄스크", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ 켈린셱타우", "→ Almaty": "→ 알마티", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 주행 10시간", "Almaty": "알마티", "Poppy fields, Merke": "양귀비 들판, 메르케", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "타라즈 · 주알리 계곡", "Shymkent": "심켄트", "Turkestan": "투르키스탄", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "우리는 아침 일곱 시에 알마티를 출발했다. 앞에는 투르키스탄까지 850킬로미터 — 나라의 절반을 가로지르는 첫 장거리 구간이 놓여 있었다. 도중에 메르케 인근의 양귀비 들판에 들렀다. 지평선까지 펼쳐진 붉은 물결, 짧은 촬영, 그리고 다시 길 위로.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "타라즈 우회로에서 든든한 점심을 먹고, 이어 그림 같은 주알리 계곡을 지났다. 굽이마다 초록빛 언덕이 잇따라 펼쳐졌다. 심켄트를 지나 마지막 구간에 들어섰다.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "열 시간의 운전 끝에 — 투르키스탄이 나타났다. 도시는 뜻밖의 모습으로 우리를 맞았다. 봉쇄된 거리, 곳곳의 경찰, 차량 행렬. 이튿날 튀르크 국가 정상회의가 준비되고 있었다. 우리는 호텔을 찾아 새벽으로 알람을 맞췄다 — 도시가 완전히 봉쇄되기 전에 떠나야 했다.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "숙박: 투르키스탄의 호텔", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "첫째 날 — 메르케 인근의 양귀비 들판과 투르키스탄으로 향하는 긴 남행길.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "투르키스탄 → 카미스티바스 호수", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · 시르다리야 삼각주로", "Kyzylorda": "키질로르다", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "코르키트 아타 묘", "Baikonur viewpoint": "바이코누르 전망지", "Lake Kamystybas": "카미스티바스 호수", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "이른 출발. 요인들이 도착하고 도시가 완전히 봉쇄되기 전에 투르키스탄을 빠져나가야 했다. 아침은 고속도로 어딘가에서 대충 해결했다. 키질로르다를 지나 — 점심, 가득 채운 연료 — 다시 북쪽으로.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "초속 20미터의 순풍이 우리를 밀어 주었다. 알고 보니 바람은 탐험 내내 변함없는 동반자가 되었다.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "우리는 코르키트 아타 기념 단지에 멈췄다 — 바람 덕분에, 공기가 옛 구조물을 지날 때 초원 자체가 노래하는 소리를 들을 수 있었다. 비행 관제 센터를 배경으로 사진 몇 장을 찍으려 바이코누르 맞은편에 한 번 더 멈췄다.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "알마티에서 이미 1,300킬로미터를 넘긴 지점에서, 우리는 시르다리야 삼각주의 시작점인 카미스티바스 호수에 닿았다. 부드러운 물, 비범한 일몰. 호숫가에 야영. 추위와 폭풍 같은 돌풍에도 우리는 수영 시즌을 열었다. 저녁, 일몰, 그리고 기대 — 내일은 아랄해의 바닥이다.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "숙박: 카미스티바스 호숫가 야영", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "둘째 날 — 코르키트 아타 묘, 바이코누르, 그리고 카미스티바스 호숫가의 야영.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "카자흐 초원은 광활하다. 제대로 가로질러 보면, 그저 창밖을 바라보는 것만으로 자기 자신의 목소리를 들을 시간을 얻게 된다.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "현장 일지 · 아랄 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "카미스티바스 → 바르사켈메스", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "아랄해 바닥 · 풍속 최대 28m/s", "Kokaral Dam": "코카랄 댐", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "아랄해 바닥 · 감시탑", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "바르사켈메스 섬", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "호숫가에서 아침을 먹고 코카랄 댐으로 향했다. 아랄해의 북쪽 부분 — 옛 면적의 약 5분의 1 — 을 구한 것이 바로 이 댐이었다. 현장의 안내판에 적힌 수치는 충격적이었다. 잃어버린 물의 양, 사라진 바다의 헥타르, 그리고 생태 재앙의 어마어마한 규모.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "이어 우리는 옛 해저를 가로질러 달렸다. 차량은 짙은 소금과 먼지 구름을 일으켰고, 바람이 그것을 사방으로 몇 킬로미터씩 흩뿌렸다. 사방이 온통 지평선. 물은 사라지고 종말 이후 같은 풍경만 남아 있었다. 우리는 관리인들이 야생동물과 화재 위험을 감시하는 감시탑에 멈췄다.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "바르사켈메스로 가는 길에 소금과 먼지 폭풍이 우리를 덮쳤다 — 시야가 50미터까지 떨어졌다. 공기 중 소금 농도가 어찌나 짙던지, 잠시 차에서 내리기만 해도 이 사이에서 모래가 서걱대는 것을 느낄 수 있었다. 두 시간 뒤, 지평선에 솟아오른 땅덩이가 나타났다. 바르사켈메스 섬 — 한때 자연보호구역이었으나, 물이 물러가면서 동물과 새들은 이미 오래전에 떠나 버렸다.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "풍속 28m/s. 우리는 보호구역 관리소에 야영을 차리고 버려진 건물들 사이에 몸을 피했다. 섬의 남쪽 끝 — 깎아지른 40미터 절벽. 그 아래에는 모래에 반쯤 묻힌 낡은 바지선이 있었고, 그 선체를 뚫고 삭사울 나무가 자라고 있었다. 북쪽에는 좌초된 배 한 척, 아직 고철 사냥꾼의 손이 닿지 않은 것. 황무지 한가운데 당당히 선, 재앙의 말 없는 증인.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "저녁이 되자 바람이 자비를 베풀어, 우리에게 모닥불과 망원경을 허락했다. 바르사켈메스는 어떤 마을에서도 멀리 떨어져 있다 — 이곳의 하늘은 빛 공해 없이 완벽하게 맑다. 별들의 우주.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "숙박: 바르사켈메스 자연보호구역 관리소", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "셋째 날 — 마른 해저를 가로질러 바르사켈메스로: 코카랄 댐, 절벽, 그리고 난파선.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "당신은 지면에서 40미터 위에 서 있고, 그 아래에서 바다는 한때 25미터 깊이로 출렁였다. 이제는 모래와 먼지 외에 아무것도 없다.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "바르사켈메스 · 셋째 날", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "바르사켈메스 → 쿨란디", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "탐험에서 가장 힘든 구간", "Western Aral Sea bed": "아랄해 서부 해저", "Bozoy": "보조이", "Kulandy village": "쿨란디 마을", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "바르사켈메스에서 야생동물을 촬영한 아침, 아침 식사, 그리고 다시 출발. 앞에는 탐험 전체에서 가장 고된 구간 — 말라붙은 바다의 서쪽 부분이 놓여 있었다. 우리는 차량과, 비교적 단단한 지면에 믿음을 걸었다. 무슨 일이라도 생기면 이 지역에서의 탈출은 거의 불가능했을 것이다.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "우리는 통과했다. 기계 고장과 까다로운 지형이 없지는 않았지만, 결국 해냈다. 단단한 도로에 올라서자 보조이로 방향을 잡았다. 도중에 말과 낙타 무리가 나타났다 — 사람이 멀지 않다는 신호였다. 보조이에서: 주유, 점심, 그리고 쿨란디로 향하는 마지막 박차.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "마을의 저녁: 바냐(증기 목욕), 게스트하우스에서의 저녁, 초원 너머의 일몰. 우리는 낙타 젖 짜는 법을 배웠고 갓 태어난 새끼들을 만났다 — 놀랍도록 사랑스러운 생명들. 우리는 오래된 집에서, 전통 코르페 이불 위에 누워 잠들었다. 감사할 만한 하루였다.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "숙박: 쿨란디 마을의 게스트하우스", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "넷째 날 — 서부 해저를 가로지르는 가장 힘든 구간, 그리고 쿨란디의 저녁.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "쿨란디 → 아랄스크", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "서쪽 해안 · 북아랄 · 항구 도시", "Kulandy": "쿨란디", "Western shore of the Aral": "아랄의 서쪽 해안", "Akespe · hot spring": "아케스페 · 온천", "Aralsk: museum & port": "아랄스크: 박물관과 항구", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "우리는 쿨란디의 주인들과 작별하고 서쪽으로 향했다 — 옛 아랄이 아직 숨 쉬는 곳으로. 날씨는 험악했다. 이슬비, 사나운 바람. 잿빛 하늘이 잿빛 풍경으로 번져 들었다.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "서쪽 해안. 물가는 수백 미터나 물러나 있었다. 우리는 부드럽고 질척한 땅을 200미터 걸어서야 물가에 닿았다. 해안에는 두꺼운 소금 거품. 바다가 어찌나 짠지 여기서는 아르테미아조차 살지 못한다. 불과 3년 전만 해도 홍학들이 이동 중에 들러 바로 그 새우를 먹었다. 이제 물은 생명을 잃어버렸다.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "우리는 북아랄로 차를 몰았다 — 구해 낸 것을 보기 위해. 아케스페 마을: 새 집들, 상점들, 가동 중인 수산 가공 공장. 바다는 그곳 사람들에게 살아갈 기회를 주었다. 온천에 몸을 담그고, 다시 아랄스크로 길을 재촉했다.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "한때 아랄해 최대의 항구였던 아랄스크는 이제 물에서 수 킬로미터 떨어져 있다. 박물관 관람, 옛 항구 산책. 녹슨 항만 크레인의 잔해는 이곳에 깊은 물과 번성한 항구가 있던 시절을 말없이 일깨운다. 게스트하우스 주인은 최근 아랄스크를 찾는 외국인 관광객이 점점 늘고 있다고 말했다 — 주민들은 거기서 새로운 생계의 길을 찾았다. 마음이 따뜻해지는 소식이었다.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "숙박: 아랄스크의 게스트하우스", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "다섯째 날 — 죽어 가는 서쪽 해안, 북아랄, 그리고 아랄스크의 옛 항구.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "바다가 죽어 가는 것을 지켜보는 일은 서글프다. 하지만 세상이 그러하다.", "The western shore · day five": "서쪽 해안 · 다섯째 날", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "아랄스크 → 켈린셱타우", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · 사막에서 산으로", "Aralsk": "아랄스크", "Karatau Mountains": "카라타우 산맥", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "켈린셱타우 산맥", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "우리는 아랄스크를 뒤로했다. 바람은 마침내 잦아들었지만, 그 대신 35도의 더위가 찾아왔다. 우리의 목적지는 카라타우 산맥. 도중에 비와 한결 시원한 공기를 만났다 — 사막의 먼지 뒤에 꼭 필요한 것이었다.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "600킬로미터를 달려, 우리는 켈린셱타우의 빼어난 봉우리들 사이에 있었다. 바위 기슭에 야영. 바람 없는 일몰 — 탐험 전체에서 처음이었다. 별들의 천장 아래에서의 훌륭한 저녁: 재앙의 가장자리에서 보낸 날들 끝의, 고요하고 사색적인 밤.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "숙박: 켈린셱타우 산중 야영", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "여섯째 날 — 사막의 더위에서 켈린셱타우의 봉우리들로.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "켈린셱타우 → 알마티", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "암각화 · 아크메시트 동굴 · 결승점", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "켈린셱타우 암각화", "Akmeshit Cave": "아크메시트 동굴", "Almaty — journey complete": "알마티 — 여정 완료", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "아침은 야영을 거두는 일로 시작되었다 — 그리고 부주의한 방문객들이 남긴 쓰레기를 줍는 일도. 그다음에는 암각화 찾기가 이어졌다. 더없이 몰입하게 하는 일이었다. 바위를 샅샅이 뒤져 고대의 새김을 찾고, 수천 년 전 한 예술가가 무엇을 그렸는지 풀어내려 애썼다. 우리의 탐색은 결실을 맺었다 — 사냥 장면, 동물의 형상, 태양 문양을 담은 스무 점이 넘는 암각화.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "다음 행선지: 아크메시트 동굴. 그 규모는 숨이 멎을 듯했다. 더욱 놀라운 것은 돌 천장 아래 어스름 속, 동굴 바닥에서 꽃을 피운 뽕나무들이었다. 인상적인 사진 몇 장을 찍고, 우리는 알마티로 방향을 잡았다.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "여정의 마지막 지점. 4천 킬로미터, 7일, 세 개의 기후대, 사라져 가는 하나의 바다 — 그리고 평생 잊지 못할 인상들.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "여정 완료 — 다시 알마티로", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "일곱째 날 — 암각화, 아크메시트 동굴, 그리고 알마티로 돌아가는 길.", "In closing": "맺으며", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "아랄해의 자취를 좇은 7일 — 끝없는 양귀비 들판에서 소금으로 뒤덮인 해안까지, 버려진 배에서 살아 있는 마을까지. 카자흐스탄은 광대하며, 그것을 진정으로 느끼려면 그저 차를 몰고 달려야 한다.", "By the numbers": "숫자로 보기", "One route, in figures": "하나의 경로, 숫자로", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "바다의 바닥에 서다", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "당신의 관심사에 맞춰 설계한 아랄 탐험", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "알마티에서 아랄의 마른 바닥까지 여러 날에 걸친 횡단 — 바르사켈메스, 난파선, 코카랄 댐, 그리고 북아랄의 살아 있는 마을들. 전용 4×4 차량, 전문 가이드, 도중의 야영과 게스트하우스.", "Explore Expeditions →": "탐험 살펴보기 →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "프라이빗 탐험 신청하기 →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.ar, {"Route": "المسار", "Day 01": "اليوم 01", "Day 02": "اليوم 02", "Day 03": "اليوم 03", "Day 04": "اليوم 04", "Day 05": "اليوم 05", "Day 06": "اليوم 06", "Day 07": "اليوم 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "يوميات ميدانية · تقرير الرحلة · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "سبعة أيام نتتبّع البحر المتلاشي", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "من حقول الخشخاش في ميركه إلى كهوف كاراتاو — يوميات ميدانية من قاع بحر آرال.", "across three regions": "عبر ثلاث مناطق", "on the road & in camp": "على الطريق وفي المخيّم", "peak wind on the seabed": "أقصى سرعة رياح على قاع البحر", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "نقوش صخرية في كيلينشكتاو", "The expedition, day by day": "الرحلة، يومًا بيوم", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "سبعة أيام، نحو أربعة آلاف كيلومتر، ثلاث مناطق وثلاثة نطاقات مناخية — وبحرٌ واحد يتلاشى في صمت. هذه يوميات رحلتنا إلى آرال عام 2026: رحلة بالسيارة عبر نصف كازاخستان للوقوف على قاع بحرٍ كان يومًا من أكبر بحيرات الأرض.", "The route · seven chapters": "المسار · سبعة فصول", "Almaty → Turkestan": "ألماتي → تركستان", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ بحيرة كاميستيباس", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ بارسا-كيلميس", "→ Kulandy": "→ كولاندي", "→ Aralsk": "→ أرالسك", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ كيلينشكتاو", "→ Almaty": "→ ألماتي", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 كم · 10 ساعات على الطريق", "Almaty": "ألماتي", "Poppy fields, Merke": "حقول الخشخاش، ميركه", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "تاراز · وادي جوالي", "Shymkent": "شيمكنت", "Turkestan": "تركستان", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "انطلقنا من ألماتي في السابعة صباحًا. أمامنا 850 كيلومترًا حتى تركستان — أول مرحلة طويلة تعبر نصف البلاد. في الطريق توقّفنا عند حقول الخشخاش قرب ميركه: أمواج من الأحمر تمتدّ إلى الأفق، جلسة تصوير سريعة، ثم عودة إلى الطريق.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "غداءٌ دسم على طريق تاراز الالتفافي، ثم عبر وادي جوالي الخلّاب، حيث تتكشّف التلال الخضراء واحدة تلو الأخرى عند كل منعطف. ومن خلال شيمكنت، بلغنا المرحلة الأخيرة.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "عشر ساعات من القيادة — وها هي تركستان. استقبلتنا المدينة على نحوٍ غير متوقّع: شوارع مغلقة بالحواجز، شرطة في كل مكان، مواكب. كانت قمّةٌ لرؤساء الدول التركية تُجهَّز لليوم التالي. وجدنا فندقنا وضبطنا المنبّه على ساعات الفجر الأولى — كان علينا المغادرة قبل أن تُغلق المدينة بالكامل.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "المبيت: فندق في تركستان", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "اليوم الأول — حقول الخشخاش قرب ميركه والطريق الجنوبي الطويل إلى تركستان.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "تركستان → بحيرة كاميستيباس", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 كم · إلى دلتا سير داريا", "Kyzylorda": "كيزيلوردا", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "ضريح قورقيت آتا", "Baikonur viewpoint": "مطلّ بايكونور", "Lake Kamystybas": "بحيرة كاميستيباس", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "انطلاقة مبكّرة. كان علينا التسلّل خارج تركستان قبل وصول كبار الضيوف وإغلاق المدينة بالكامل. تناولنا الفطور على عجل في مكان ما على الطريق السريع. عبر كيزيلوردا — غداء، خزّان ممتلئ — ثم شمالًا.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "دفعتنا ريحٌ خلفية بسرعة 20 م/ث. وكما اتّضح لاحقًا، صارت الريح رفيقًا دائمًا طوال الرحلة بأكملها.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "توقّفنا عند مجمّع ضريح قورقيت آتا — وبفضل الريح، كان بإمكانك سماع السهوب نفسها تغنّي حين يمرّ الهواء عبر المنشآت القديمة. توقّفٌ آخر مقابل بايكونور لالتقاط بضع صور بخلفية مركز التحكّم بالرحلات.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "وقد قطعنا أكثر من 1300 كيلومتر من ألماتي، وصلنا إلى بحيرة كاميستيباس — بداية دلتا سير داريا. ماءٌ عذب، وغروبٌ استثنائي. مخيّم على الشاطئ. افتتحنا موسم السباحة رغم البرد والعواصف الهوجاء. عشاء، غروب، وترقّب: غدًا، قاع بحر آرال.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "المبيت: مخيّم بري على شاطئ بحيرة كاميستيباس", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "اليوم الثاني — ضريح قورقيت آتا، وبايكونور، والمخيّم على شاطئ بحيرة كاميستيباس.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "السهوب الكازاخية شاسعة. اعبُرها كما ينبغي، فتجد متّسعًا من الوقت لتُصغي إلى نفسك — بمجرّد النظر من النافذة.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "يوميات ميدانية · آرال 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "كاميستيباس → بارسا-كيلميس", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "قاع بحر آرال · رياح تصل إلى 28 م/ث", "Kokaral Dam": "سدّ كوكارال", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "قاع آرال · برج مراقبة", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "جزيرة بارسا-كيلميس", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "فطورٌ على ضفّة البحيرة، ثم انطلاقٌ نحو سدّ كوكارال. هذا السدّ بالذات هو الذي أنقذ الجزء الشمالي من بحر آرال — نحو خُمس مساحته السابقة. عرضت لوحة معلومات في الموقع الأرقام، وكانت مذهلة: كمّيات المياه المفقودة، وهكتارات البحر المتلاشية، وحجم الكارثة البيئية الهائل.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "ثم قُدنا عبر قاع البحر السابق. أثارت المركبات سُحبًا كثيفة من الملح والغبار، نثرتها الريح كيلومترات في كل اتجاه. أفقٌ في كل مكان. رحل الماء تاركًا وراءه مشاهد أشبه بما بعد نهاية العالم. توقّفنا عند برج مراقبة يستخدمه الحرّاس لرصد الحياة البرّية ومخاطر الحرائق.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "في الطريق إلى بارسا-كيلميس، غمرتنا عاصفة من الملح والغبار — هبط مدى الرؤية إلى خمسين مترًا. كان تركيز الملح في الهواء شديدًا إلى حدّ أنك بعد خروجك من المركبة للحظة، تشعر بالحصى يتقرمش بين أسنانك. وبعد ساعتين، ظهرت كتلة يابسة مرتفعة في الأفق. جزيرة بارسا-كيلميس: كانت يومًا محمية طبيعية، هربت منها الحيوانات والطيور منذ زمن طويل مع انحسار الماء.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "ريحٌ بسرعة 28 م/ث. نصبنا المخيّم عند محطة حرّاس المحمية، محتمين بين مبانٍ مهجورة. الطرف الجنوبي للجزيرة — منحدرات شاهقة بارتفاع أربعين مترًا؛ وعند سفحها صندلٌ قديم نصف مدفون في الرمل، تنمو أشجار الساكسول عبر هيكله. وإلى الشمال، سفينة جنحت إلى البرّ، لم يصل إليها بعد صائدو الخردة المعدنية. شاهدٌ صامت على الكارثة، يقف شامخًا في وسط القفر.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "ومع المساء، رقّت الريح، فمنحتنا نار مخيّم وتلسكوبًا. تقع بارسا-كيلميس بعيدًا عن أي مستوطنة — فالسماء هنا صافية تمامًا، خالية من التلوّث الضوئي. كونٌ من النجوم.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "المبيت: محطة حرّاس محمية بارسا-كيلميس الطبيعية", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "اليوم الثالث — عبر قاع البحر الجافّ إلى بارسا-كيلميس: سدّ كوكارال، والمنحدرات، وحطام السفينة.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "أنت واقفٌ على ارتفاع أربعين مترًا فوق الأرض، وتحتك كان البحر يلاطم يومًا على عمق خمسة وعشرين مترًا. أما الآن فلا شيء سوى الرمل والغبار.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "بارسا-كيلميس · اليوم الثالث", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "بارسا-كيلميس → كولاندي", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "أصعب مراحل الرحلة", "Western Aral Sea bed": "قاع آرال الغربي", "Bozoy": "بوزوي", "Kulandy village": "قرية كولاندي", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "صباحٌ من تصوير الحياة البرّية في بارسا-كيلميس، ثم فطور، ثم انطلاق. أمامنا كان أشقّ مقطع في الرحلة بأكملها: الجزء الغربي من البحر الجافّ. وضعنا ثقتنا في المركبات وفي الأرض الصلبة نسبيًا. ولو حدث أي خطب، لكان الإخلاء من هذه الأنحاء شبه مستحيل.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "نجحنا في العبور. لم يخلُ الأمر من أعطال ميكانيكية وتضاريس صعبة، لكننا نجحنا. وما إن بلغنا طريقًا صلبًا حتى اتّجهنا نحو بوزوي. في الطريق ظهرت قطعان من الخيول والإبل — دليلٌ على أن الناس ليسوا بعيدين. في بوزوي: تزوّد بالوقود، وغداء، ودفعة أخيرة إلى كولاندي.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "مساءٌ في القرية: حمّام بخار، وعشاء في بيت الضيافة، وغروب فوق السهوب. تعلّمنا حلب الإبل والتقينا بمواليد صغيرة — مخلوقات محبّبة إلى حدّ مدهش. خلدنا إلى النوم في بيت قديم، فوق لُحُف الكورپه التقليدية. يومٌ يستحقّ الامتنان.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "المبيت: بيت ضيافة في قرية كولاندي", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "اليوم الرابع — أصعب مرحلة عبر القاع الغربي، ومساء في كولاندي.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "كولاندي → أرالسك", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "الشاطئ الغربي · آرال الشمالي · مدينة الميناء", "Kulandy": "كولاندي", "Western shore of the Aral": "الشاطئ الغربي لآرال", "Akespe · hot spring": "أكيسبه · ينبوع حار", "Aralsk: museum & port": "أرالسك: المتحف والميناء", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "ودّعنا مضيفينا في كولاندي واتّجهنا غربًا — إلى حيث ما زال آرال القديم يتنفّس. كان الطقس كريهًا: رذاذ، وريحٌ عاتية. سماءٌ رمادية تذوب في مشهدٍ رمادي.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "الشاطئ الغربي. تراجع خطّ الماء مئات الأمتار. مشينا مئتي متر على الأقدام فوق أرض طريّة مشبعة بالماء لنبلغ حافّة الماء. وعند الشاطئ — رغوة كثيفة من الملح. البحر شديد الملوحة حتى إن جمبري الملح نفسه لا يعيش هنا. قبل ثلاث سنوات فقط، كانت طيور النحام تتوقّف في هجرتها لتتغذّى على ذلك الجمبري بالذات. أما الآن فقد غدا الماء بلا حياة.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "تابعنا القيادة إلى آرال الشمالي — لنرى ما الذي أُنقِذ. قرية أكيسبه: بيوت جديدة، متاجر، ومصنع لمعالجة الأسماك يعمل بكامل طاقته. لقد منح البحر أهل المكان فرصةً للمضيّ قُدُمًا. اغتسلنا في ينبوع حار، ثم واصلنا إلى أرالسك.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "كانت أرالسك يومًا أكبر ميناء على بحر آرال، وهي تقف اليوم على بُعد كيلومترات من الماء. جولة في المتحف، ومشيٌ في الميناء القديم. تقف هياكل رافعات الميناء الصدئة تذكيرًا صامتًا بزمنٍ كان فيه هنا ماءٌ عميق وميناءٌ مزدهر. أخبرنا صاحب بيت الضيافة أن المزيد من السيّاح الأجانب صاروا يزورون أرالسك مؤخّرًا — وقد وجد الأهالي في ذلك مصدر رزقٍ جديدًا. خبرٌ يثلج الصدر.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "المبيت: بيت ضيافة في أرالسك", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "اليوم الخامس — الشاطئ الغربي المحتضر، وآرال الشمالي، وميناء أرالسك القديم.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "إنه لأمرٌ يبعث على الأسى أن ترى بحرًا يموت. لكن هكذا تجري الأمور.", "The western shore · day five": "الشاطئ الغربي · اليوم الخامس", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "أرالسك → كيلينشكتاو", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 كم · من الصحراء إلى الجبال", "Aralsk": "أرالسك", "Karatau Mountains": "جبال كاراتاو", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "جبال كيلينشكتاو", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "تركنا أرالسك خلفنا. هدأت الريح أخيرًا، لكن حلّ محلّها حرٌّ بلغ خمسًا وثلاثين درجة. وجهتنا: جبال كاراتاو. في الطريق صادفنا مطرًا وهواءً أبرد — وهو تمامًا ما كنّا بحاجة إليه بعد غبار الصحراء.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "ستمئة كيلومتر، ووجدنا أنفسنا بين قمم كيلينشكتاو الخلّابة. مخيّمٌ عند سفح الصخور. غروبٌ بلا ريح — الأول في الرحلة بأكملها. عشاءٌ طيّب تحت قبّة من النجوم: أمسيةٌ هادئة متأمّلة بعد أيام قُضِيت على حافة الكارثة.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "المبيت: مخيّم بري في جبال كيلينشكتاو", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "اليوم السادس — من حرّ الصحراء إلى قمم كيلينشكتاو.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "كيلينشكتاو → ألماتي", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "نقوش صخرية · كهف أكميشيت · خطّ النهاية", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "نقوش كيلينشكتاو الصخرية", "Akmeshit Cave": "كهف أكميشيت", "Almaty — journey complete": "ألماتي — اكتملت الرحلة", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "بدأ الصباح بتفكيك المخيّم — وجمع النفايات التي خلّفها زوّار غير مبالين. ثم جاء البحث عن النقوش الصخرية. مسعى آسرٌ تمامًا: تفتيش الصخور بحثًا عن نقوش قديمة، ومحاولة فكّ ما صوّره فنّانٌ قبل آلاف السنين. أثمر بحثنا — أكثر من عشرين نقشًا صخريًا تصوّر مشاهد صيد وأشكال حيوانات ورموزًا شمسية.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "المحطة التالية: كهف أكميشيت. كان حجمه يحبس الأنفاس. والأكثر إدهاشًا أشجار التوت المزهرة على أرض الكهف، في الضوء الخافت تحت القبو الصخري. بضع صور لافتة، ثم اتّجهنا صوب ألماتي.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "النقطة الأخيرة في الرحلة. أربعة آلاف كيلومتر، سبعة أيام، ثلاثة نطاقات مناخية، بحرٌ واحد يتلاشى — وانطباعاتٌ تكفي العمر كلّه.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "اكتملت الرحلة — عودة إلى ألماتي", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "اليوم السابع — النقوش الصخرية، وكهف أكميشيت، وطريق العودة إلى ألماتي.", "In closing": "في الختام", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "سبعة أيام في إثر بحر آرال — من حقول الخشخاش اللامتناهية إلى شواطئ تكسوها قشور الملح، ومن سفنٍ مهجورة إلى قرى نابضة بالحياة. كازاخستان شاسعة، ولتشعر بها حقًّا، ما عليك إلا أن تقود.", "By the numbers": "بالأرقام", "One route, in figures": "مسارٌ واحد بالأرقام", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "قِف على قاع البحر", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "رحلة إلى آرال، مصمّمة وفق اهتماماتك", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "رحلة عبور تمتدّ عدّة أيام من ألماتي إلى قاع آرال الجافّ — بارسا-كيلميس، وحطام السفن، وسدّ كوكارال، وقرى آرال الشمالي النابضة بالحياة. نقل خاصّ بمركبات دفع رباعي، ومرشدون متخصّصون، ومخيّمات برّية وبيوت ضيافة على طول الطريق.", "Explore Expeditions →": "استكشف الرحلات →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "اطلب رحلة خاصة →"});
Object.assign(window.I18N.es, {"Route": "Ruta", "Day 01": "Día 01", "Day 02": "Día 02", "Day 03": "Día 03", "Day 04": "Día 04", "Day 05": "Día 05", "Day 06": "Día 06", "Day 07": "Día 07", "Field Journal · Expedition Report · 2026": "Diario de campo · Informe de expedición · 2026", "Seven days tracing the vanishing sea": "Siete días tras las huellas del mar que desaparece", "From the poppy fields of Merke to the caves of Karatau — a field journal from the bed of the Aral Sea.": "De los campos de amapolas de Merke a las cuevas de Karatau: un diario de campo desde el lecho del mar de Aral.", "across three regions": "a través de tres regiones", "on the road & in camp": "en ruta y en campamento", "peak wind on the seabed": "viento máximo en el lecho marino", "petroglyphs at Kelinshektau": "petroglifos en Kelinshektau", "The expedition, day by day": "La expedición, día a día", "Seven days, around four thousand kilometres, three regions and three climate zones — and one sea that is quietly disappearing. This is the journal of our 2026 Aral expedition: a drive across half of Kazakhstan to stand on the bed of a sea that was once one of the largest lakes on Earth.": "Siete días, unos cuatro mil kilómetros, tres regiones y tres zonas climáticas, y un mar que desaparece en silencio. Este es el diario de nuestra expedición al Aral 2026: un viaje a través de medio Kazajistán para pisar el lecho de un mar que alguna vez fue uno de los lagos más grandes de la Tierra.", "The route · seven chapters": "La ruta · siete capítulos", "Almaty → Turkestan": "Almaty → Turkestán", "→ Lake Kamystybas": "→ lago Kamystybás", "→ Barsa-Kelmes": "→ Barsa-Kelmes", "→ Kulandy": "→ Kulandy", "→ Aralsk": "→ Aralsk", "→ Kelinshektau": "→ Kelinshektau", "→ Almaty": "→ Almaty", "≈ 850 km · 10 hours on the road": "≈ 850 km · 10 horas de camino", "Almaty": "Almaty", "Poppy fields, Merke": "Campos de amapolas, Merke", "Taraz · Zhualin Valley": "Taraz · valle de Zhualy", "Shymkent": "Shymkent", "Turkestan": "Turkestán", "We set off from Almaty at seven in the morning. Ahead of us lay 850 kilometres to Turkestan — the first long haul across half the country. Along the way, we stopped at the poppy fields near Merke: waves of red stretching to the horizon, a quick photo session, and back on the road.": "Partimos de Almaty a las siete de la mañana. Por delante teníamos 850 kilómetros hasta Turkestán: la primera etapa larga a través de medio país. En el camino paramos en los campos de amapolas cerca de Merke: olas de rojo hasta el horizonte, una breve sesión de fotos y de nuevo a la carretera.", "A hearty lunch on the Taraz bypass, then through the picturesque Zhualin Valley, where green hills unfold one after another around every bend. Through Shymkent, we joined the final stretch.": "Un almuerzo copioso en la circunvalación de Taraz, y luego por el pintoresco valle de Zhualy, donde las colinas verdes se suceden una tras otra en cada curva. Pasando por Shymkent, nos incorporamos al tramo final.", "Ten hours of driving — and there it was, Turkestan. The city greeted us unexpectedly: barricaded streets, police everywhere, motorcades. A summit of Turkic heads of state was being prepared for the following day. We found our hotel and set the alarm for the small hours — we needed to leave before the city was sealed off entirely.": "Diez horas de conducción, y ahí estaba, Turkestán. La ciudad nos recibió de forma inesperada: calles cortadas, policía por todas partes, caravanas. Para el día siguiente se preparaba una cumbre de jefes de Estado de los pueblos túrquicos. Encontramos el hotel y pusimos el despertador de madrugada: teníamos que salir antes de que cerraran la ciudad por completo.", "Overnight: hotel in Turkestan": "Noche: hotel en Turkestán", "Day one — the poppy fields near Merke and the long road south to Turkestan.": "Día uno: los campos de amapolas cerca de Merke y la larga carretera hacia el sur hasta Turkestán.", "Turkestan → Lake Kamystybas": "Turkestán → lago Kamystybás", "≈ 700 km · into the Syr Darya delta": "≈ 700 km · hacia el delta del Sir Daria", "Kyzylorda": "Kyzylorda", "Korkyt Ata Memorial": "Mausoleo de Korkyt Ata", "Baikonur viewpoint": "mirador de Baikonur", "Lake Kamystybas": "lago Kamystybás", "An early start. We needed to slip out of Turkestan before the dignitaries arrived and the city locked down completely. Breakfast was grabbed somewhere on the highway. Through Kyzylorda — lunch, a full tank — and onwards north.": "Salida temprana. Teníamos que escabullirnos de Turkestán antes de que llegaran los dignatarios y la ciudad quedara totalmente bloqueada. El desayuno lo cogimos en algún punto de la carretera. Por Kyzylorda: almuerzo, depósito lleno, y rumbo al norte.", "A tailwind of 20 m/s pushed us along. As it turned out, the wind would become a constant companion for the entire expedition.": "Un viento de cola de 20 m/s nos empujaba. Resultó que el viento se convertiría en compañero constante durante toda la expedición.", "We paused at the Korkyt Ata memorial complex — thanks to the wind, you could hear the steppe itself singing as air passed through the ancient structures. Another stop opposite Baikonur for a couple of photographs with the Mission Control Centre in the background.": "Nos detuvimos en el complejo memorial de Korkyt Ata: gracias al viento, se oía cantar a la propia estepa cuando el aire atravesaba las antiguas estructuras. Otra parada frente a Baikonur para un par de fotos con el Centro de Control al fondo.", "Already over 1,300 kilometres from Almaty, we arrived at Lake Kamystybas — the beginning of the Syr Darya delta. Soft water, extraordinary sunsets. Camp on the shore. We opened the swimming season despite the chill and gale-force gusts. Supper, sunset, anticipation: tomorrow, the bed of the Aral Sea.": "Ya a más de 1.300 kilómetros de Almaty, llegamos al lago Kamystybás, el inicio del delta del Sir Daria. Agua suave, atardeceres extraordinarios. Campamento en la orilla. Inauguramos la temporada de baño pese al frío y las ráfagas huracanadas. Cena, atardecer, expectación: mañana, el lecho del mar de Aral.", "Overnight: wild camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas": "Noche: campamento libre en la orilla del lago Kamystybás", "Day two — the Korkyt Ata memorial, Baikonur, and camp on the shore of Lake Kamystybas.": "Día dos: el memorial de Korkyt Ata, Baikonur y el campamento en la orilla del lago Kamystybás.", "The Kazakh steppe is vast. Drive through it properly, and you find the time to hear yourself — simply by gazing out of the window.": "La estepa kazaja es inmensa. Atraviésala como es debido y encontrarás el tiempo de escucharte a ti mismo, simplemente mirando por la ventanilla.", "Field Journal · Aral 2026": "Diario de campo · Aral 2026", "Kamystybas → Barsa-Kelmes": "Kamystybás → Barsa-Kelmes", "The Aral Sea bed · winds up to 28 m/s": "El lecho del mar de Aral · vientos de hasta 28 m/s", "Kokaral Dam": "Presa de Kokaral", "Aral Sea bed · tower": "Lecho del Aral · torre", "Barsa-Kelmes Island": "Isla de Barsa-Kelmes", "Breakfast on the lakeshore, then off to the Kokaral Dam. It was this dam that saved the northern portion of the Aral Sea — roughly a fifth of its former area. An information board at the site laid out the figures, and they were staggering: volumes of water lost, hectares of sea vanished, the sheer scale of the ecological catastrophe.": "Desayuno a la orilla del lago y luego rumbo a la presa de Kokaral. Fue esta presa la que salvó la parte norte del mar de Aral, alrededor de una quinta parte de su antigua superficie. Un panel informativo exponía las cifras, y eran abrumadoras: volúmenes de agua perdidos, hectáreas de mar desaparecidas, la magnitud misma de la catástrofe ecológica.", "Then we drove across the former seabed. The vehicles raised dense clouds of salt and dust, scattered by the wind for kilometres in every direction. Horizon all around. The water had gone, leaving post-apocalyptic landscapes in its wake. We stopped at an observation tower used by wardens to monitor wildlife and fire hazards.": "Luego condujimos por el antiguo lecho marino. Los vehículos levantaban densas nubes de sal y polvo que el viento esparcía kilómetros en todas direcciones. Horizonte por todas partes. El agua se había ido, dejando tras de sí paisajes posapocalípticos. Nos detuvimos en una torre de observación que usan los guardas para vigilar la fauna y el riesgo de incendios.", "On the way to Barsa-Kelmes, a salt-and-dust storm engulfed us — visibility dropped to fifty metres. The salt concentration in the air was so intense that after stepping out of the vehicle for a moment, you could feel the grit crunching between your teeth. Two hours later, a raised landmass appeared on the horizon. Barsa-Kelmes Island: once a nature reserve, from which animals and birds had long since fled as the water retreated.": "Camino de Barsa-Kelmes nos envolvió una tormenta de sal y polvo: la visibilidad cayó a cincuenta metros. La concentración de sal en el aire era tan intensa que, al bajar un instante del vehículo, se notaba la arenilla crujir entre los dientes. Dos horas después, una masa de tierra elevada apareció en el horizonte. La isla de Barsa-Kelmes: en otro tiempo una reserva natural de la que animales y aves habían huido hacía mucho a medida que el agua se retiraba.", "Wind at 28 m/s. We pitched camp at the reserve's ranger station, sheltering amongst abandoned buildings. The island's southern edge — sheer forty-metre cliffs; at the foot, an old barge half-buried in sand, with saxaul trees growing through its hull. To the north, a ship run aground, not yet reached by scrap-metal hunters. A silent witness to catastrophe, standing proud in the middle of the wasteland.": "Viento de 28 m/s. Acampamos en la estación de guardas de la reserva, al amparo de edificios abandonados. El borde sur de la isla: acantilados verticales de cuarenta metros; al pie, una vieja barcaza medio enterrada en la arena, con saxaules creciendo a través de su casco. Al norte, un barco encallado, aún no alcanzado por los cazadores de chatarra. Un testigo silencioso de la catástrofe, erguido con orgullo en mitad del páramo.", "Come evening, the wind showed mercy, granting us a campfire and a telescope. Barsa-Kelmes lies far from any settlement — the sky here is perfectly clear, free of light pollution. A universe of stars.": "Al caer la tarde, el viento se apiadó y nos concedió una hoguera y un telescopio. Barsa-Kelmes está lejos de cualquier asentamiento: aquí el cielo es perfectamente nítido, libre de contaminación lumínica. Un universo de estrellas.", "Overnight: Barsa-Kelmes Nature Reserve ranger station": "Noche: estación de guardas de la Reserva Natural de Barsa-Kelmes", "Day three — across the dry seabed to Barsa-Kelmes: the Kokaral Dam, the cliffs, and the shipwreck.": "Día tres: a través del lecho seco hasta Barsa-Kelmes: la presa de Kokaral, los acantilados y el pecio.", "You are standing forty metres above the ground, and beneath you the sea once lapped at a depth of twenty-five metres. Now there is nothing but sand and dust.": "Estás a cuarenta metros sobre el suelo, y bajo tus pies el mar batía antaño a veinticinco metros de profundidad. Ahora no hay más que arena y polvo.", "Barsa-Kelmes · day three": "Barsa-Kelmes · día tres", "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy": "Barsa-Kelmes → Kulandy", "The hardest leg of the expedition": "La etapa más dura de la expedición", "Western Aral Sea bed": "Lecho occidental del Aral", "Bozoy": "Bozoy", "Kulandy village": "aldea de Kulandy", "A morning of wildlife photography on Barsa-Kelmes, breakfast, and then onwards. Ahead lay the most gruelling stretch of the entire expedition: the western portion of the dried-out sea. We placed our faith in the vehicles and the relatively firm ground. If anything went wrong, evacuation from these parts would be nigh on impossible.": "Una mañana de fotografía de fauna en Barsa-Kelmes, desayuno, y luego adelante. Por delante teníamos el tramo más extenuante de toda la expedición: la parte occidental del mar secado. Pusimos nuestra fe en los vehículos y en el suelo relativamente firme. Si algo salía mal, la evacuación de estos parajes sería casi imposible.", "We made it through. Not without mechanical hiccups and some tricky terrain, but we made it. Once on solid road, we set course for Bozoy. Along the way, herds of horses and camels appeared — a sign that people were not far off. In Bozoy: a refuel, lunch, and a final push to Kulandy.": "Lo logramos. No sin contratiempos mecánicos y algún terreno traicionero, pero lo logramos. Ya en carretera firme, pusimos rumbo a Bozoy. En el camino aparecieron manadas de caballos y camellos, señal de que la gente no estaba lejos. En Bozoy: repostaje, almuerzo y un último empujón hasta Kulandy.", "Evening in the aul: a banya, supper at the guesthouse, sunset over the steppe. We learnt to milk camels and met newborn calves — remarkably endearing creatures. We fell asleep in an old house, on traditional korpe quilts. A day to be grateful for.": "Tarde en el aúl: un banya, cena en la casa de huéspedes, atardecer sobre la estepa. Aprendimos a ordeñar camellas y conocimos crías recién nacidas, criaturas extraordinariamente entrañables. Nos dormimos en una vieja casa, sobre korpes tradicionales. Un día para agradecer.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Kulandy village": "Noche: casa de huéspedes en la aldea de Kulandy", "Day four — the hardest leg across the western seabed, and evening in Kulandy.": "Día cuatro: la etapa más dura por el lecho occidental y la tarde en Kulandy.", "Kulandy → Aralsk": "Kulandy → Aralsk", "Western shore · North Aral · the port town": "Orilla occidental · Aral del Norte · la ciudad portuaria", "Kulandy": "Kulandy", "Western shore of the Aral": "Orilla occidental del Aral", "Akespe · hot spring": "Akespe · fuente termal", "Aralsk: museum & port": "Aralsk: museo y puerto", "We bade farewell to our hosts in Kulandy and headed west — to where the old Aral still draws breath. The weather was foul: drizzle, fierce wind. A grey sky bleeding into a grey landscape.": "Nos despedimos de nuestros anfitriones en Kulandy y partimos hacia el oeste, allí donde el viejo Aral todavía respira. El tiempo era horrible: llovizna, viento feroz. Un cielo gris que se fundía en un paisaje gris.", "The western shore. The waterline had retreated by hundreds of metres. We walked two hundred metres on foot across soft, sodden ground to reach the water's edge. At the shore — a thick foam of salt. The sea is so saline that not even brine shrimp survive here. Just three years ago, flamingos used to stop on their migration and feed on those very shrimp. Now the water has become lifeless.": "La orilla occidental. La línea del agua había retrocedido cientos de metros. Caminamos doscientos metros a pie sobre un suelo blando y empapado para llegar a la orilla del agua. En la orilla, una espesa espuma de sal. El mar es tan salino que aquí ni siquiera sobreviven las artemias. Hace apenas tres años, los flamencos se detenían en su migración para alimentarse precisamente de esos crustáceos. Ahora el agua se ha vuelto sin vida.", "We drove on to the North Aral — to see what had been saved. Akespe village: new houses, shops, a functioning fish-processing plant. The sea had given the local people a chance to carry on. We bathed in a hot spring, then pressed on to Aralsk.": "Seguimos hacia el Aral del Norte, para ver lo que se había salvado. La aldea de Akespe: casas nuevas, tiendas, una planta procesadora de pescado en funcionamiento. El mar había dado a la población local una oportunidad de seguir adelante. Nos bañamos en una fuente termal y luego apretamos hasta Aralsk.", "Once the largest port on the Aral Sea, Aralsk now stands kilometres from the water. A tour of the museum, a walk through the old harbour. The rusting hulks of port cranes stand as a silent reminder of a time when there was deep water and a thriving port here. The guesthouse owner told us that more and more foreign tourists have been visiting Aralsk lately — and the locals have found in this a new source of livelihood. Heartening news.": "Antaño el mayor puerto del mar de Aral, Aralsk se halla hoy a kilómetros del agua. Una visita al museo, un paseo por el viejo puerto. Los esqueletos oxidados de las grúas portuarias son un recordatorio silencioso de un tiempo en que aquí había aguas profundas y un puerto próspero. El dueño de la casa de huéspedes nos contó que últimamente cada vez más turistas extranjeros visitan Aralsk, y que los lugareños han hallado en ello una nueva fuente de sustento. Una noticia alentadora.", "Overnight: guesthouse in Aralsk": "Noche: casa de huéspedes en Aralsk", "Day five — the dying western shore, the North Aral, and the old port of Aralsk.": "Día cinco: la moribunda orilla occidental, el Aral del Norte y el viejo puerto de Aralsk.", "It is a melancholy thing, to watch a sea die. But so it goes.": "Es algo melancólico ver morir un mar. Pero así son las cosas.", "The western shore · day five": "La orilla occidental · día cinco", "Aralsk → Kelinshektau": "Aralsk → Kelinshektau", "≈ 600 km · from desert to mountains": "≈ 600 km · del desierto a las montañas", "Aralsk": "Aralsk", "Karatau Mountains": "Montes Karatau", "Kelinshektau Mountains": "Montes Kelinshektau", "We left Aralsk behind. The wind had finally died down, only to be replaced by thirty-five-degree heat. Our heading: the Karatau Mountains. Along the road we met rain and cooler air — just what was needed after the desert dust.": "Dejamos Aralsk atrás. El viento por fin había amainado, solo para ser sustituido por un calor de treinta y cinco grados. Nuestro rumbo: los montes Karatau. En el camino encontramos lluvia y aire más fresco, justo lo que hacía falta tras el polvo del desierto.", "Six hundred kilometres, and we found ourselves amongst the scenic peaks of Kelinshektau. Camp at the foot of the rocks. A sunset without wind — the first of the entire expedition. A fine supper beneath a canopy of stars: a quiet, contemplative evening after days spent on the edge of catastrophe.": "Seiscientos kilómetros, y nos encontramos entre los pintorescos picos de Kelinshektau. Campamento al pie de las rocas. Un atardecer sin viento, el primero de toda la expedición. Una buena cena bajo una bóveda de estrellas: una velada tranquila y contemplativa tras días pasados al borde de la catástrofe.", "Overnight: wild camp in the Kelinshektau Mountains": "Noche: campamento libre en los montes Kelinshektau", "Day six — from desert heat into the peaks of Kelinshektau.": "Día seis: del calor del desierto a los picos de Kelinshektau.", "Kelinshektau → Almaty": "Kelinshektau → Almaty", "Petroglyphs · Akmeshit Cave · the finish": "Petroglifos · cueva de Akmeshit · la meta", "Kelinshektau petroglyphs": "Petroglifos de Kelinshektau", "Akmeshit Cave": "Cueva de Akmeshit", "Almaty — journey complete": "Almaty — viaje completado", "The morning began with breaking camp — and collecting the litter left behind by careless visitors. Then came the hunt for petroglyphs. A thoroughly absorbing pursuit: scouring the rocks for ancient carvings and trying to decipher what an artist depicted thousands of years ago. Our hunt proved fruitful — over twenty petroglyphs depicting hunting scenes, animal figures, and solar symbols.": "La mañana empezó levantando el campamento, y recogiendo la basura que habían dejado visitantes descuidados. Luego llegó la búsqueda de petroglifos. Una tarea absolutamente absorbente: rastrear las rocas en busca de grabados antiguos e intentar descifrar qué representó un artista hace miles de años. Nuestra búsqueda fue fructífera: más de veinte petroglifos con escenas de caza, figuras de animales y símbolos solares.", "Next stop: Akmeshit Cave. The scale was breathtaking. Even more astonishing were the mulberry trees in bloom on the cave floor, in the half-light beneath the stone vault. A few striking photographs, and we set our course for Almaty.": "Siguiente parada: la cueva de Akmeshit. Su escala quitaba el aliento. Aún más asombrosos eran los morales en flor en el suelo de la cueva, en la penumbra bajo la bóveda de piedra. Unas cuantas fotos impactantes, y pusimos rumbo a Almaty.", "The final point of the journey. Four thousand kilometres, seven days, three climate zones, one vanishing sea — and a lifetime of impressions.": "El punto final del viaje. Cuatro mil kilómetros, siete días, tres zonas climáticas, un mar que desaparece, y recuerdos para toda la vida.", "Journey complete — back in Almaty": "Viaje completado — de vuelta en Almaty", "Day seven — petroglyphs, Akmeshit Cave, and the road home to Almaty.": "Día siete: petroglifos, la cueva de Akmeshit y el camino de regreso a Almaty.", "In closing": "Para terminar", "Seven days in the wake of the Aral Sea — from boundless poppy fields to salt-encrusted shores, from abandoned ships to living villages. Kazakhstan is immense, and to truly feel it, you simply have to drive.": "Siete días tras la estela del mar de Aral: de campos de amapolas sin fin a orillas costradas de sal, de barcos abandonados a aldeas llenas de vida. Kazajistán es inmenso, y para sentirlo de verdad solo hay que conducir.", "By the numbers": "En cifras", "One route, in figures": "Una ruta en cifras", "Stand on the bed of the sea": "Pisa el lecho del mar", "An Aral expedition, designed around your interests": "Una expedición al Aral, diseñada a la medida de tus intereses", "A multi-day traverse from Almaty to the dry bed of the Aral — Barsa-Kelmes, the shipwrecks, the Kokaral Dam, and the living villages of the North Aral. Private 4×4 transport, specialist guides, wild camps and guesthouses along the way.": "Una travesía de varios días desde Almaty hasta el lecho seco del Aral: Barsa-Kelmes, los pecios, la presa de Kokaral y las aldeas vivas del Aral del Norte. Transporte privado en 4×4, guías especializados, campamentos libres y casas de huéspedes a lo largo del recorrido.", "Explore Expeditions →": "Explorar expediciones →", "Request a Private Expedition →": "Solicitar una expedición privada →"});


/* === Site coverage gap-fill translations === */
Object.assign(window.I18N.ru, {"Trust — a direct operator, not a contractor": "Доверие — мы прямой оператор, а не посредник", "Team — every journey has been field-tested": "Команда — каждый маршрут проверен в поле", "Sustainability — travel that gives back to the land": "Устойчивость — путешествия, что отдают земле", "Nothing about the country had been allowed to actually": "Ничему о стране не позволяли по-настоящему", "This page has moved. If you are not redirected automatically,": "Эта страница переехала. Если перенаправление не произошло автоматически,", "click here": "нажмите здесь", "British researcher, Fellow of the Royal Geographical Society, and author of": "Британский исследователь, член Королевского географического общества, автор книг", "and": "и", "2-day Escape · Year-round": "2-дневный выезд · круглый год", "Altyn-Emel — 2-Day Desert & Dune Expedition": "Алтын-Эмель — 2-дневная экспедиция по пустыне и дюнам", "Singing Dune · Aktau": "Поющий бархан · Актау", "← Back to Escapes": "← Назад к выездам", "Connectivity": "Связь", "Digital detox": "Цифровой детокс", "Far enough to leave the city behind, close enough for a weekend out.": "Достаточно далеко, чтобы оставить город позади, достаточно близко для выходных.", "bands": "полос", "The park holds the Singing Dune (150 m barchan with acoustic properties), the Oshaktas menhirs, Kosbastau sacred springs (a 700-year-old willow, radon waters), the Katutau volcanic mountains (300-million-year-old basalt), and the Aktau coloured range — twenty distinct mineral bands in white, red, ochre and blue. Night one is a wild camp under Altyn-Emel's deep sky.": "В парке есть Поющий бархан (150-метровый бархан с акустическими свойствами), менгиры Ошақтас, священные источники Косбастау (700-летняя ива, радоновые воды), вулканические горы Катутау (базальт возрастом 300 миллионов лет) и цветные горы Актау — двадцать отчётливых минеральных полос белого, красного, охристого и синего цвета. Первая ночь — дикий лагерь под глубоким небом Алтын-Эмеля.", "from $340": "от $340", "2-day Escape · April–October · YurtaDa Charyn": "2-дневный выезд · апрель–октябрь · YurtaDa Чарын", "from $360": "от $360", "2-day Escape · May–October": "2-дневный выезд · май–октябрь", "from $410": "от $410", "from $250": "от $250", "1 night in nomadic yurt at YurtaDa Kargaly": "1 ночь в кочевой юрте в YurtaDa Каргалы", "All meals: welcome tea, dinner, breakfast, farewell lunch": "Всё питание: приветственный чай, ужин, завтрак, прощальный обед", "Cultural programme: eagle handling, archery, horsemanship": "Культурная программа: соколиная охота, стрельба из лука, верховая езда", "1–2 bilingual Dala Arba guides": "1–2 двуязычных гида Dala Arba", "6 – 10 days": "6–10 дней", "3-day Journey · Year-round": "3-дневное путешествие · круглый год", "← Back to Journeys": "← Назад к путешествиям", "Under the Milky Way": "Под Млечным Путём", "from $480": "от $480", "Mountain Trek · 5 days · July–August only": "Горный трек · 5 дней · только июль–август", "Assy Plateau to Kolsai Lakes — 5-Day Mountain Trek": "Плато Ассы — Кольсайские озёра — 5-дневный горный трек", "July–August only": "только июль–август", "3,010 m (Kyzylauuz Pass)": "3 010 м (перевал Кызылауыз)", "kg": "кг", "Day 00": "День 00", "Almaty → Assy Plateau (140 km, 3.5 hrs via Turgen Gorge).": "Алматы → плато Ассы (140 км, 3,5 ч через Тургенское ущелье).", "Camp setup at base (~2,600 m). Briefing & gear check.": "Установка лагеря на базе (~2 600 м). Брифинг и проверка снаряжения.", "from $890": "от $890", "Grand Expedition · 10 days · Spring / Autumn": "Большая экспедиция · 10 дней · весна / осень", "Great Kazakhstan Expedition — Part III: From the Caspian to the Mountains": "Великая казахстанская экспедиция — Часть III: От Каспия до гор", "from $2,050": "от $2 050", "5-day Journey · May–October · Almaty · Assy · Charyn · Tekes · Khan Tengri": "5-дневное путешествие · май–октябрь · Алматы · Ассы · Чарын · Текес · Хан-Тенгри", "Arrival Almaty.": "Прибытие в Алматы.", "from $820": "от $820", "Expedition · 8 days · Spring / Autumn": "Экспедиция · 8 дней · весна / осень", "Great Kazakhstan Expedition — Part II: From Sea to Sea": "Великая казахстанская экспедиция — Часть II: От моря до моря", "Bozzhyra — chalk spires of a 65-million-year-old Cretaceous ocean floor, most otherworldly landscape in Kazakhstan": "Бозжыра — меловые шпили дна мелового океана возрастом 65 миллионов лет, самый неземной пейзаж Казахстана", "Beket Ata Underground Mosque (1780) — sacred Sufi site carved into chalk cliffs, thousands of pilgrims annually": "Подземная мечеть Бекет-Ата (1780) — священное суфийское место, вырубленное в меловых скалах, тысячи паломников ежегодно", "Ustyurt Plateau — ~400 km crossing of one of the world's last great wildernesses": "Плато Устюрт — переход ~400 км через одну из последних великих пустынь мира", "Kyzylkup \"Tiramisu\" — layered red & white chalk, shark teeth fossils from the ancient Tethys Sea": "Кызылкуп «Тирамису» — слоистый красно-белый мел, окаменелые зубы акул из древнего океана Тетис", "Andrey Astafyev (Day 6) — expert archaeologist on Kyzylkala fortress and Zoroastrian nomadic sites": "Андрей Астафьев (день 6) — археолог-эксперт по крепости Кызылкала и зороастрийским кочевым памятникам", "Blue Bay Caspian — first sight of blue water after days of chalk and salt desert": "Голубая бухта Каспия — первый вид синей воды после дней мела и солончаков", "~500 km north through the Syr Darya delta to the dam that brought the Small Aral back.": "~500 км на север через дельту Сырдарьи к плотине, вернувшей Малый Арал.", "from $1,640": "от $1 640", "Terms & Conditions": "Условия и положения", "These terms govern the use of dalaarba.com and the booking of expeditions and journeys with DALA ARBA Expeditions. By submitting an inquiry or making a booking, you agree to these terms.": "Настоящие условия регулируют использование сайта dalaarba.com и бронирование экспедиций и путешествий с DALA ARBA Expeditions. Отправляя запрос или оформляя бронирование, вы соглашаетесь с этими условиями.", "Inquiries & quotes": "Запросы и расчёты", "All journeys are private and bespoke. Prices shown on the site are indicative, per person and depend on group size, season and route. A binding price is confirmed in a written proposal.": "Все путешествия частные и индивидуальные. Цены на сайте ориентировочны, указаны на человека и зависят от размера группы, сезона и маршрута. Окончательная цена подтверждается в письменном предложении.", "Booking & payment": "Бронирование и оплата", "A booking is confirmed once a deposit is received against an agreed proposal. Payment schedule, balance due dates and accepted methods are set out in your individual proposal.": "Бронирование подтверждается после получения депозита по согласованному предложению. График платежей, сроки оплаты остатка и принимаемые способы оплаты указаны в вашем индивидуальном предложении.", "Cancellations & changes": "Отмены и изменения", "Cancellation and amendment terms are specified in your proposal. Because expeditions involve advance commitments to camps, permits and transport, cancellation fees may apply.": "Условия отмены и изменений указаны в вашем предложении. Поскольку экспедиции связаны с предварительными обязательствами по лагерям, разрешениям и транспорту, может взиматься плата за отмену.", "Travel insurance, visas & borders": "Страховка, визы и границы", "Comprehensive travel insurance with medical-evacuation cover is required for all guests. Guests are responsible for holding valid passports and any visas required for the countries on their route; we assist with border registration where applicable.": "Для всех гостей обязательна полная туристическая страховка с покрытием медицинской эвакуации. Гости несут ответственность за наличие действующих паспортов и любых виз, необходимых для стран по маршруту; мы помогаем с пограничной регистрацией там, где это применимо.", "Risk & liability": "Риски и ответственность", "Expedition travel takes place in remote environments and carries inherent risks. We operate to professional safety standards, but guests participate at their own risk and must follow guide instructions. Our liability is limited to the extent permitted by applicable law.": "Экспедиционные путешествия проходят в удалённых районах и сопряжены с неотъемлемыми рисками. Мы работаем по профессиональным стандартам безопасности, но гости участвуют на свой риск и обязаны следовать указаниям гида. Наша ответственность ограничена в пределах, допустимых применимым правом.", "Force majeure": "Форс-мажор", "We are not liable for failure to perform due to events beyond our reasonable control, including weather, border closures, natural events or political disruption. We will work to offer reasonable alternatives.": "Мы не несём ответственности за неисполнение обязательств вследствие событий вне нашего разумного контроля, включая погоду, закрытие границ, стихийные явления или политические потрясения. Мы будем стремиться предложить разумные альтернативы.", "Governing law": "Применимое право", "These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kazakhstan.": "Настоящие условия регулируются законодательством Республики Казахстан.", "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan ·": "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Алматы, Казахстан ·", "These terms are provided as a general template and should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication.": "Эти условия представлены как общий шаблон и должны быть проверены квалифицированным юристом перед публикацией."});
Object.assign(window.I18N.kk, {"Trust — a direct operator, not a contractor": "Сенім — біз делдал емес, тікелей оператор", "Team — every journey has been field-tested": "Команда — әр маршрут далада сыналған", "Sustainability — travel that gives back to the land": "Тұрақтылық — жерге қайтаратын саяхат", "Nothing about the country had been allowed to actually": "Ел туралы ештеңеге шынымен рұқсат етілмеген еді", "This page has moved. If you are not redirected automatically,": "Бұл бет көшірілді. Егер автоматты түрде бағытталмасаңыз,", "click here": "осы жерді басыңыз", "British researcher, Fellow of the Royal Geographical Society, and author of": "Британдық зерттеуші, Корольдік география қоғамының мүшесі, кітаптардың авторы", "and": "және", "2-day Escape · Year-round": "2 күндік демалыс · жыл бойы", "Altyn-Emel — 2-Day Desert & Dune Expedition": "Алтын-Емел — 2 күндік шөл мен құмбел экспедициясы", "Singing Dune · Aktau": "Әнші құм · Ақтау", "← Back to Escapes": "← Демалыстарға қайту", "Connectivity": "Байланыс", "Digital detox": "Цифрлық детокс", "Far enough to leave the city behind, close enough for a weekend out.": "Қаланы артта қалдыруға жеткілікті алыс, демалыс күніне жеткілікті жақын.", "bands": "белдеу", "The park holds the Singing Dune (150 m barchan with acoustic properties), the Oshaktas menhirs, Kosbastau sacred springs (a 700-year-old willow, radon waters), the Katutau volcanic mountains (300-million-year-old basalt), and the Aktau coloured range — twenty distinct mineral bands in white, red, ochre and blue. Night one is a wild camp under Altyn-Emel's deep sky.": "Саябақта Әнші құм (акустикалық қасиеті бар 150 метрлік құмбел), Ошақтас мензирлері, Қосбастау қасиетті бұлақтары (700 жылдық тал, радонды су), Қатутау жанартау таулары (300 миллион жылдық базальт) және Ақтау түрлі-түсті жоталары бар — ақ, қызыл, сары және көк түсті жиырма айқын минералды белдеу. Бірінші түн — Алтын-Емелдің терең аспаны астындағы дала лагері.", "from $340": "$340-дан бастап", "2-day Escape · April–October · YurtaDa Charyn": "2 күндік демалыс · сәуір–қазан · YurtaDa Шарын", "from $360": "$360-дан бастап", "2-day Escape · May–October": "2 күндік демалыс · мамыр–қазан", "from $410": "$410-дан бастап", "from $250": "$250-ден бастап", "1 night in nomadic yurt at YurtaDa Kargaly": "YurtaDa Қарғалыдағы көшпелі киіз үйде 1 түн", "All meals: welcome tea, dinner, breakfast, farewell lunch": "Барлық тамақ: қарсы алу шайы, кешкі ас, таңғы ас, қоштасу түскі асы", "Cultural programme: eagle handling, archery, horsemanship": "Мәдени бағдарлама: бүркіт салу, садақ ату, ат спорты", "1–2 bilingual Dala Arba guides": "1–2 екі тілді Dala Arba гиді", "6 – 10 days": "6–10 күн", "3-day Journey · Year-round": "3 күндік саяхат · жыл бойы", "← Back to Journeys": "← Саяхаттарға қайту", "Under the Milky Way": "Құс жолының астында", "from $480": "$480-ден бастап", "Mountain Trek · 5 days · July–August only": "Таулы трек · 5 күн · тек шілде–тамыз", "Assy Plateau to Kolsai Lakes — 5-Day Mountain Trek": "Асы үстірті — Көлсай көлдері — 5 күндік таулы трек", "July–August only": "тек шілде–тамыз", "3,010 m (Kyzylauuz Pass)": "3 010 м (Қызылауыз асуы)", "kg": "кг", "Day 00": "00-күн", "Almaty → Assy Plateau (140 km, 3.5 hrs via Turgen Gorge).": "Алматы → Асы үстірті (140 км, 3,5 сағ Түрген шатқалы арқылы).", "Camp setup at base (~2,600 m). Briefing & gear check.": "Базада лагерь құру (~2 600 м). Брифинг және жабдықты тексеру.", "from $890": "$890-нан бастап", "Grand Expedition · 10 days · Spring / Autumn": "Үлкен экспедиция · 10 күн · көктем / күз", "Great Kazakhstan Expedition — Part III: From the Caspian to the Mountains": "Ұлы Қазақстан экспедициясы — III бөлім: Каспийден тауларға дейін", "from $2,050": "$2 050-ден бастап", "5-day Journey · May–October · Almaty · Assy · Charyn · Tekes · Khan Tengri": "5 күндік саяхат · мамыр–қазан · Алматы · Асы · Шарын · Текес · Хан Тәңірі", "Arrival Almaty.": "Алматыға келу.", "from $820": "$820-ден бастап", "Expedition · 8 days · Spring / Autumn": "Экспедиция · 8 күн · көктем / күз", "Great Kazakhstan Expedition — Part II: From Sea to Sea": "Ұлы Қазақстан экспедициясы — II бөлім: Теңізден теңізге", "Bozzhyra — chalk spires of a 65-million-year-old Cretaceous ocean floor, most otherworldly landscape in Kazakhstan": "Бозжыра — 65 миллион жылдық бор дәуірі мұхит түбінің бор шыңдары, Қазақстандағы ең ғаламшардан тыс пейзаж", "Beket Ata Underground Mosque (1780) — sacred Sufi site carved into chalk cliffs, thousands of pilgrims annually": "Бекет Ата жерасты мешіті (1780) — бор жартастарына қашалған қасиетті сопылық орын, жыл сайын мыңдаған қажы", "Ustyurt Plateau — ~400 km crossing of one of the world's last great wildernesses": "Үстірт үстірті — әлемдегі соңғы ұлы жабайы жерлердің бірі арқылы ~400 км өту", "Kyzylkup \"Tiramisu\" — layered red & white chalk, shark teeth fossils from the ancient Tethys Sea": "Қызылқұп «Тирамису» — қабат-қабат қызыл-ақ бор, ежелгі Тетис теңізінің акула тістерінің қазбалары", "Andrey Astafyev (Day 6) — expert archaeologist on Kyzylkala fortress and Zoroastrian nomadic sites": "Андрей Астафьев (6-күн) — Қызылқала қамалы мен зороастрлық көшпелі ескерткіштер жөніндегі археолог-сарапшы", "Blue Bay Caspian — first sight of blue water after days of chalk and salt desert": "Көк шығанақ Каспий — бор мен тұзды шөл күндерінен кейін көк судың алғашқы көрінісі", "~500 km north through the Syr Darya delta to the dam that brought the Small Aral back.": "Сырдария атырауы арқылы солтүстікке ~500 км, Кіші Аралды қайтарған бөгетке дейін.", "from $1,640": "$1 640-тан бастап", "Terms & Conditions": "Шарттар мен ережелер", "These terms govern the use of dalaarba.com and the booking of expeditions and journeys with DALA ARBA Expeditions. By submitting an inquiry or making a booking, you agree to these terms.": "Осы шарттар dalaarba.com сайтын пайдалануды және DALA ARBA Expeditions компаниясымен экспедициялар мен саяхаттарды брондауды реттейді. Сұраныс жіберу немесе брондау жасау арқылы сіз осы шарттармен келісесіз.", "Inquiries & quotes": "Сұраныстар мен есептеулер", "All journeys are private and bespoke. Prices shown on the site are indicative, per person and depend on group size, season and route. A binding price is confirmed in a written proposal.": "Барлық саяхаттар жеке және жекелей жасалады. Сайттағы бағалар бағдарлы, бір адамға есептелген және топ көлеміне, маусымға және маршрутқа байланысты. Түпкілікті баға жазбаша ұсыныста расталады.", "Booking & payment": "Брондау және төлем", "A booking is confirmed once a deposit is received against an agreed proposal. Payment schedule, balance due dates and accepted methods are set out in your individual proposal.": "Брондау келісілген ұсыныс бойынша депозит алынғаннан кейін расталады. Төлем кестесі, қалдықты төлеу мерзімдері және қабылданатын тәсілдер сіздің жеке ұсынысыңызда көрсетіледі.", "Cancellations & changes": "Болдырмау және өзгерістер", "Cancellation and amendment terms are specified in your proposal. Because expeditions involve advance commitments to camps, permits and transport, cancellation fees may apply.": "Болдырмау және өзгерту шарттары сіздің ұсынысыңызда көрсетіледі. Экспедициялар лагерьлер, рұқсаттар және көлік бойынша алдын ала міндеттемелерді қамтитындықтан, болдырмау үшін ақы алынуы мүмкін.", "Travel insurance, visas & borders": "Сақтандыру, визалар және шекаралар", "Comprehensive travel insurance with medical-evacuation cover is required for all guests. Guests are responsible for holding valid passports and any visas required for the countries on their route; we assist with border registration where applicable.": "Барлық қонақтар үшін медициналық эвакуацияны қамтитын толық туристік сақтандыру міндетті. Қонақтар жарамды паспорттар мен маршруттағы елдерге қажетті визаларды иеленуге жауапты; біз қажет болған жерде шекарада тіркеуге көмектесеміз.", "Risk & liability": "Тәуекел және жауапкершілік", "Expedition travel takes place in remote environments and carries inherent risks. We operate to professional safety standards, but guests participate at their own risk and must follow guide instructions. Our liability is limited to the extent permitted by applicable law.": "Экспедициялық саяхаттар шалғай жерлерде өтеді және өзіне тән тәуекелдерге ие. Біз кәсіби қауіпсіздік стандарттары бойынша жұмыс істейміз, бірақ қонақтар өз тәуекелімен қатысады және гидтің нұсқауларын орындауға міндетті. Біздің жауапкершілігіміз қолданыстағы заңмен рұқсат етілген шекте шектеледі.", "Force majeure": "Форс-мажор", "We are not liable for failure to perform due to events beyond our reasonable control, including weather, border closures, natural events or political disruption. We will work to offer reasonable alternatives.": "Біз ауа райы, шекараның жабылуы, табиғи құбылыстар немесе саяси тұрақсыздық сияқты ақылға қонымды бақылауымыздан тыс оқиғалардан туындаған міндеттемелерді орындамағанымыз үшін жауап бермейміз. Біз ақылға қонымды баламалар ұсынуға тырысамыз.", "Governing law": "Қолданыстағы заң", "These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kazakhstan.": "Осы шарттар Қазақстан Республикасының заңдарымен реттеледі.", "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan ·": "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Алматы, Қазақстан ·", "These terms are provided as a general template and should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication.": "Бұл шарттар жалпы үлгі ретінде ұсынылған және жариялау алдында білікті заңгердің тексеруінен өтуі тиіс."});
