Object.assign(window.I18N.kk, {"Expedition Report · Aral Sea": "Экспедиция есебі · Арал теңізі", "Kazakh Carpet Museum (Shymkent)": "Қазақ кілем мұражайы (Шымкент)", "Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "Тоқыма мұрасы және көшпелі рәміздер", "06 — Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "06 — Тоқыма мұрасы және көшпелі рәміздер", "05 — Cultural heritage partner": "05 — Мәдени мұра серіктесі", "Lived in, not performed": "Өмір сүріп жатыр, қойылым емес", "Carpets as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge — symbolism, history, and cultural memory woven into wool.": "Кілемдер — көшпелі білімнің көрнекі мұрағаты: жүнге тоқылған рәміздер, тарих және мәдени жады.", "Researcher of Kazakh carpet heritage · Founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum, Shymkent · Languages: Kazakh, Russian": "Қазақ кілем мұрасының зерттеушісі · Шымкенттегі Қазақ кілем мұражайының негізін қалаушы · Тілдер: қазақ, орыс", "How we use it": "Біз оны қалай пайдаланамыз", "What we collect": "Біз нені жинаймыз", "Your rights": "Сіздің құқықтарыңыз", "Sharing": "Бөлісу", "Cookies & analytics": "Cookie файлдары және аналитика", "Last updated: June 2026": "Соңғы жаңарту: 2026 жылғы маусым", "Legal": "Құқықтық ақпарат", "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan": "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Алматы, Қазақстан", "from $1,040": "$1 040-тан бастап", "DALA ARBA Expeditions respects your privacy. This page explains what information we collect when you use dalaarba.com and how we handle it.": "DALA ARBA Expeditions сіздің құпиялылығыңызды құрметтейді. Бұл бетте dalaarba.com сайтын пайдаланғанда қандай ақпарат жинайтынымыз және оны қалай өңдейтініміз түсіндіріледі.", "How we collect, use and protect your information.": "Ақпаратыңызды қалай жинайтынымыз, пайдаланатынымыз және қорғайтынымыз.", "When you submit an inquiry through our planning form or contact us by email or WhatsApp, we collect the details you provide — typically your name, email address, phone number, travel dates, group size and trip preferences. We also collect basic, anonymous usage statistics, such as pages visited, to improve the site.": "Жоспарлау формасы арқылы сұраныс жібергенде немесе электрондық пошта не WhatsApp арқылы бізге хабарласқанда, біз сіз ұсынған мәліметтерді жинаймыз — әдетте есіміңіз, электрондық пошта мекенжайыңыз, телефон нөміріңіз, саяхат күндеріңіз, топ көлемі және сапар қалаулары. Сондай-ақ сайтты жақсарту үшін негізгі, анонимді пайдалану статистикасын (мысалы, қаралған беттер) жинаймыз.", "We use your information solely to respond to your inquiry, design and operate your expedition, and send you proposals and trip-related communication. We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your consent.": "Біз ақпаратыңызды тек сұранысыңызға жауап беру, экспедицияңызды әзірлеу мен ұйымдастыру және сізге ұсыныстар мен сапарға қатысты хабарламалар жіберу үшін пайдаланамыз. Біз деректеріңізді сатпаймыз және келісіміңізсіз оны бөгде маркетинг үшін қолданбаймыз.", "We share your details only with the local guides, camps and service partners required to deliver your trip, and only to the extent necessary. We may share information where required by law.": "Біз мәліметтеріңізді тек сапарыңызды жүзеге асыру үшін қажетті жергілікті гидтермен, лагерьлермен және сервистік серіктестермен, әрі тек қажетті көлемде бөлісеміз. Заң талап еткен жағдайда ақпаратты беруіміз мүмкін.", "The site may use privacy-respecting analytics and a language-preference cookie. You can control cookies through your browser settings.": "Сайт құпиялылықты құрметтейтін аналитиканы және тіл таңдауын сақтайтын cookie файлын пайдалануы мүмкін. Cookie файлдарын браузер баптаулары арқылы басқара аласыз.", "You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal information we hold about you. To do so, contact us at": "Сіз туралы сақтайтын жеке ақпаратқа қол жеткізуді, оны түзетуді немесе жоюды сұрай аласыз. Ол үшін бізге мына мекенжай арқылы хабарласыңыз:", "Four thousand kilometres, three regions, one disappearing sea. A day-by-day journal from the poppy fields of Merke to the shipwrecks of Barsa-Kelmes and the caves of Karatau.": "Төрт мың шақырым, үш өңір, жоғалып бара жатқан бір теңіз. Меркенің көкнәр алқаптарынан Барсакелместің батқан кемелеріне және Қаратау үңгірлеріне дейінгі күнделік.", "Located in the historic center of Shymkent, the Kazakh Carpet Museum is a unique cultural space dedicated to the preservation and interpretation of Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Created from a private collection, the museum houses one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Шымкенттің тарихи орталығында орналасқан Қазақ кілем мұражайы — Қазақстанның тоқыма мұрасын сақтау мен таныстыруға арналған бірегей мәдени кеңістік. Жеке коллекциядан құрылған мұражайда елдегі дәстүрлі қазақ кілемдерінің ең үлкен жинақтарының бірі сақталады.", "Here, carpets are seen not only as works of decorative art, but as carriers of worldview, symbolism, historical memory, and nomadic knowledge. The museum's signature is an open-air courtyard exhibition, where the ornaments of historic carpets are reproduced on its walls and railings, turning the space into a museum under the open sky.": "Мұнда кілемдер тек сәндік өнер туындысы ретінде ғана емес, дүниетаным, рәміз, тарихи жады және көшпелі білімнің тасымалдаушысы ретінде қарастырылады. Мұражайдың айрықша белгісі — ашық аспан астындағы аула көрмесі, мұнда тарихи кілемдердің оюлары қабырғалар мен қоршауларда қайталанып, кеңістікті ашық аспан астындағы мұражайға айналдырады.", "Beyond its collection, the museum serves as a living laboratory of nomadic symbolism, where carpets are presented not only as decorative objects but as carriers of history, belief systems, social memory, and traditional knowledge. A distinctive feature of the museum is its outdoor artistic installation, where large-scale reproductions of historic carpet designs transform the surrounding courtyard into an open-air exhibition space.": "Жинағынан бөлек, мұражай көшпелі рәміздердің тірі зертханасы қызметін атқарады, мұнда кілемдер тек сәндік зат ретінде емес, тарих, наным жүйесі, әлеуметтік жады және дәстүрлі білімнің тасымалдаушысы ретінде ұсынылады. Мұражайдың айрықша ерекшелігі — оның ашық ауадағы көркем инсталляциясы, мұнда тарихи кілем өрнектерінің ауқымды көшірмелері айналадағы ауланы ашық аспан астындағы көрме кеңістігіне айналдырады.", "The Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent is a unique cultural space dedicated to preserving and promoting Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Built from a private collection, it holds one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Шымкенттегі Қазақ кілем мұражайы — Қазақстанның тоқыма мұрасын сақтау мен насихаттауға арналған бірегей мәдени кеңістік. Жеке коллекциядан құрылған ол елдегі дәстүрлі қазақ кілемдерінің ең үлкен жинақтарының бірін сақтайды.", "Dana Erik is a Kazakh researcher, collector, and cultural advocate dedicated to preserving and interpreting the heritage of traditional Kazakh carpets. For more than a decade, she has documented, collected, and studied historic carpets, ornaments, and textile traditions, viewing them as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge, symbolism, and cultural memory.": "Дана Ерік — дәстүрлі қазақ кілемдерінің мұрасын сақтау мен таныстыруға арналған қазақ зерттеушісі, коллекционер және мәдениет жанашыры. Он жылдан астам уақыт бойы ол тарихи кілемдерді, оюларды және тоқыма дәстүрлерін құжаттап, жинап, зерттеп келеді, оларды көшпелі білім, рәміз және мәдени жадының көрнекі мұрағаты ретінде қарастырады.", "Dana's work focuses on decoding the symbolic language of Kazakh ornamentation and promoting the revival of traditional carpet weaving as an important element of Kazakhstan's cultural identity. Through exhibitions, lectures, research, and public engagement, she continues to advocate for the preservation of one of the oldest artistic traditions of the Great Steppe.": "Дананың жұмысы қазақ оюларының рәміздік тілін ашуға және дәстүрлі кілем тоқуды Қазақстан мәдени бірегейлігінің маңызды элементі ретінде қайта жаңғыртуды насихаттауға бағытталған. Көрмелер, дәрістер, зерттеулер және қоғаммен жұмыс арқылы ол Ұлы дала өнерінің ең көне дәстүрлерінің бірін сақтауды жақтауды жалғастыруда.", "She is the founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent, the first private museum of its kind in Kazakhstan. Her collection includes more than 1,000 historic carpets, alongside traditional chests, yurt elements, musical instruments, and other ethnographic artifacts.": "Ол — Қазақстандағы өз түріндегі алғашқы жеке мұражай болып табылатын Шымкенттегі Қазақ кілем мұражайының негізін қалаушы. Оның коллекциясында 1000-нан астам тарихи кілеммен қатар дәстүрлі сандықтар, киіз үй бөлшектері, музыкалық аспаптар және басқа этнографиялық бұйымдар бар.", "These are not museum dioramas. Each YurtaDa is a living cultural environment at one of our four destinations, hosted by people from the local community — families who have belonged to these landscapes for generations.": "Бұл мұражай диорамалары емес. Әрбір YurtaDa — біздің төрт бағытымыздың бірінде орналасқан тірі мәдени орта, оны жергілікті қауымнан шыққан адамдар — ұрпақтан-ұрпаққа осы өлкеге тиесілі отбасылар қабылдайды.", "You sleep in a yurt with modern comfort, eat what has been cooked here for centuries, and meet the craftspeople, musicians, and riders who call this place home — not performing for visitors, but simply living their traditions.": "Сіз заманауи жайлылығы бар киіз үйде ұйықтайсыз, ғасырлар бойы осында пісіріліп келген тағамды жейсіз және осы жерді өз үйім деп санайтын шеберлермен, әншілермен және салт аттылармен танысасыз — олар келушілерге қойылым көрсетпейді, тек өз дәстүрлерімен өмір сүреді.", "YurtaDa is the name for each of Dala Arba's ethno-village anchor points — and the philosophy that shapes them. A YurtaDa is a traditional Kazakh settlement: yurts, a shared fire, and a rhythm of life set by the land and the seasons.": "YurtaDa — Dala Arba-ның әрбір этно-ауыл тірек нүктесінің атауы әрі оларды қалыптастыратын философия. YurtaDa — дәстүрлі қазақ қонысы: киіз үйлер, ортақ от және жер мен маусымдар белгілейтін өмір ырғағы."});
Object.assign(window.I18N.de, {"Expedition Report · Aral Sea": "Expeditionsbericht · Aralsee", "YurtaDa · Charyn Canyon": "YurtaDa · Charyn-Schlucht", "YurtaDa · Kargaly": "YurtaDa · Kargaly", "Kazakh Carpet Museum (Shymkent)": "Kasachisches Teppichmuseum (Schymkent)", "Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "Textilerbe & nomadische Symbolik", "06 — Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "06 — Textilerbe & nomadische Symbolik", "03 — Camps": "03 — Camps", "05 — Cultural heritage partner": "05 — Partner für Kulturerbe", "Lived in, not performed": "Gelebt, nicht aufgeführt", "Carpets as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge — symbolism, history, and cultural memory woven into wool.": "Teppiche als visuelles Archiv nomadischen Wissens — Symbolik, Geschichte und kulturelles Gedächtnis, in Wolle gewoben.", "Researcher of Kazakh carpet heritage · Founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum, Shymkent · Languages: Kazakh, Russian": "Forscherin des kasachischen Teppicherbes · Gründerin des Kasachischen Teppichmuseums, Schymkent · Sprachen: Kasachisch, Russisch", "How we use it": "Wie wir sie verwenden", "What we collect": "Was wir erfassen", "Your rights": "Ihre Rechte", "Sharing": "Weitergabe", "Cookies & analytics": "Cookies & Analyse", "Last updated: June 2026": "Zuletzt aktualisiert: Juni 2026", "Legal": "Rechtliches", "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan": "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kasachstan", "Format": "Format", "Region": "Region", "Journal": "Journal", "Mission": "Mission", "Team": "Team", "Steppe": "Steppe", "Park": "Park", "Lead": "Lead", "Editorial": "Editorial", "Support": "Support", "Expedition": "Expedition", "Max 12": "Max 12", "Jun – Sep": "Jun – Sep", "Jun–Sep": "Jun–Sep", "September 2026": "September 2026", "DALA ARBA Expeditions respects your privacy. This page explains what information we collect when you use dalaarba.com and how we handle it.": "DALA ARBA Expeditions respektiert Ihre Privatsphäre. Diese Seite erläutert, welche Informationen wir bei der Nutzung von dalaarba.com erfassen und wie wir damit umgehen.", "How we collect, use and protect your information.": "Wie wir Ihre Informationen erfassen, verwenden und schützen.", "When you submit an inquiry through our planning form or contact us by email or WhatsApp, we collect the details you provide — typically your name, email address, phone number, travel dates, group size and trip preferences. We also collect basic, anonymous usage statistics, such as pages visited, to improve the site.": "Wenn Sie über unser Planungsformular eine Anfrage senden oder uns per E-Mail oder WhatsApp kontaktieren, erfassen wir die von Ihnen angegebenen Daten — in der Regel Name, E-Mail-Adresse, Telefonnummer, Reisedaten, Gruppengröße und Reisewünsche. Außerdem erfassen wir grundlegende, anonyme Nutzungsstatistiken wie besuchte Seiten, um die Website zu verbessern.", "We use your information solely to respond to your inquiry, design and operate your expedition, and send you proposals and trip-related communication. We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your consent.": "Wir verwenden Ihre Informationen ausschließlich, um auf Ihre Anfrage zu antworten, Ihre Expedition zu gestalten und durchzuführen und Ihnen Angebote sowie reisebezogene Mitteilungen zu senden. Wir verkaufen Ihre Daten nicht und nutzen sie ohne Ihre Einwilligung nicht für fremdes Marketing.", "We share your details only with the local guides, camps and service partners required to deliver your trip, and only to the extent necessary. We may share information where required by law.": "Wir geben Ihre Daten nur an die lokalen Guides, Camps und Servicepartner weiter, die zur Durchführung Ihrer Reise erforderlich sind, und nur im notwendigen Umfang. Wir geben Informationen weiter, wenn dies gesetzlich vorgeschrieben ist.", "The site may use privacy-respecting analytics and a language-preference cookie. You can control cookies through your browser settings.": "Die Website kann datenschutzfreundliche Analysen und ein Cookie für die Sprachpräferenz verwenden. Cookies können Sie über die Einstellungen Ihres Browsers steuern.", "You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal information we hold about you. To do so, contact us at": "Sie können Auskunft über die von uns gespeicherten personenbezogenen Daten verlangen sowie deren Berichtigung oder Löschung. Kontaktieren Sie uns dazu unter", "Four thousand kilometres, three regions, one disappearing sea. A day-by-day journal from the poppy fields of Merke to the shipwrecks of Barsa-Kelmes and the caves of Karatau.": "Viertausend Kilometer, drei Regionen, ein verschwindendes Meer. Ein Tag-für-Tag-Tagebuch von den Mohnfeldern bei Merke bis zu den Schiffswracks von Barsa-Kelmes und den Höhlen des Karatau.", "Located in the historic center of Shymkent, the Kazakh Carpet Museum is a unique cultural space dedicated to the preservation and interpretation of Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Created from a private collection, the museum houses one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Im historischen Zentrum von Schymkent gelegen, ist das Kasachische Teppichmuseum ein einzigartiger Kulturraum, der dem Bewahren und Deuten des Textilerbes Kasachstans gewidmet ist. Aus einer Privatsammlung hervorgegangen, beherbergt das Museum eine der größten Sammlungen traditioneller kasachischer Teppiche des Landes.", "Here, carpets are seen not only as works of decorative art, but as carriers of worldview, symbolism, historical memory, and nomadic knowledge. The museum's signature is an open-air courtyard exhibition, where the ornaments of historic carpets are reproduced on its walls and railings, turning the space into a museum under the open sky.": "Hier werden Teppiche nicht nur als dekorative Kunstwerke gesehen, sondern als Träger von Weltbild, Symbolik, historischem Gedächtnis und nomadischem Wissen. Das Markenzeichen des Museums ist eine Hofausstellung unter freiem Himmel, in der die Ornamente historischer Teppiche an Wänden und Geländern nachgebildet werden und den Raum in ein Museum unter freiem Himmel verwandeln.", "Beyond its collection, the museum serves as a living laboratory of nomadic symbolism, where carpets are presented not only as decorative objects but as carriers of history, belief systems, social memory, and traditional knowledge. A distinctive feature of the museum is its outdoor artistic installation, where large-scale reproductions of historic carpet designs transform the surrounding courtyard into an open-air exhibition space.": "Über seine Sammlung hinaus dient das Museum als lebendiges Labor nomadischer Symbolik, in dem Teppiche nicht nur als dekorative Objekte, sondern als Träger von Geschichte, Glaubenssystemen, sozialem Gedächtnis und traditionellem Wissen präsentiert werden. Ein besonderes Merkmal ist die künstlerische Außeninstallation, bei der großformatige Reproduktionen historischer Teppichmuster den umliegenden Hof in einen Ausstellungsraum unter freiem Himmel verwandeln.", "The Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent is a unique cultural space dedicated to preserving and promoting Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Built from a private collection, it holds one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Das Kasachische Teppichmuseum in Schymkent ist ein einzigartiger Kulturraum, der dem Bewahren und Fördern des Textilerbes Kasachstans gewidmet ist. Aus einer Privatsammlung entstanden, beherbergt es eine der größten Sammlungen traditioneller kasachischer Teppiche des Landes.", "Dana Erik is a Kazakh researcher, collector, and cultural advocate dedicated to preserving and interpreting the heritage of traditional Kazakh carpets. For more than a decade, she has documented, collected, and studied historic carpets, ornaments, and textile traditions, viewing them as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge, symbolism, and cultural memory.": "Dana Erik ist eine kasachische Forscherin, Sammlerin und Kulturfürsprecherin, die sich dem Bewahren und Deuten des Erbes traditioneller kasachischer Teppiche widmet. Seit mehr als einem Jahrzehnt dokumentiert, sammelt und erforscht sie historische Teppiche, Ornamente und Textiltraditionen und betrachtet sie als visuelles Archiv nomadischen Wissens, nomadischer Symbolik und kulturellen Gedächtnisses.", "Dana's work focuses on decoding the symbolic language of Kazakh ornamentation and promoting the revival of traditional carpet weaving as an important element of Kazakhstan's cultural identity. Through exhibitions, lectures, research, and public engagement, she continues to advocate for the preservation of one of the oldest artistic traditions of the Great Steppe.": "Danas Arbeit konzentriert sich darauf, die symbolische Sprache der kasachischen Ornamentik zu entschlüsseln und die Wiederbelebung der traditionellen Teppichweberei als wichtiges Element der kulturellen Identität Kasachstans zu fördern. Durch Ausstellungen, Vorträge, Forschung und öffentliches Engagement setzt sie sich weiterhin für die Bewahrung einer der ältesten künstlerischen Traditionen der Großen Steppe ein.", "She is the founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent, the first private museum of its kind in Kazakhstan. Her collection includes more than 1,000 historic carpets, alongside traditional chests, yurt elements, musical instruments, and other ethnographic artifacts.": "Sie ist die Gründerin des Kasachischen Teppichmuseums in Schymkent, des ersten Privatmuseums seiner Art in Kasachstan. Ihre Sammlung umfasst mehr als 1.000 historische Teppiche, dazu traditionelle Truhen, Jurtenelemente, Musikinstrumente und weitere ethnografische Artefakte.", "These are not museum dioramas. Each YurtaDa is a living cultural environment at one of our four destinations, hosted by people from the local community — families who have belonged to these landscapes for generations.": "Dies sind keine Museumsdioramen. Jedes YurtaDa ist eine lebendige kulturelle Umgebung an einem unserer vier Reiseziele, betreut von Menschen aus der örtlichen Gemeinschaft — Familien, die seit Generationen zu diesen Landschaften gehören.", "You sleep in a yurt with modern comfort, eat what has been cooked here for centuries, and meet the craftspeople, musicians, and riders who call this place home — not performing for visitors, but simply living their traditions.": "Sie schlafen in einer Jurte mit modernem Komfort, essen, was hier seit Jahrhunderten gekocht wird, und treffen die Handwerker, Musiker und Reiter, die diesen Ort ihr Zuhause nennen — sie führen nichts für Besucher auf, sondern leben einfach ihre Traditionen.", "YurtaDa is the name for each of Dala Arba's ethno-village anchor points — and the philosophy that shapes them. A YurtaDa is a traditional Kazakh settlement: yurts, a shared fire, and a rhythm of life set by the land and the seasons.": "YurtaDa ist der Name für jeden der Ethno-Dorf-Ankerpunkte von Dala Arba — und die Philosophie, die sie prägt. Ein YurtaDa ist eine traditionelle kasachische Siedlung: Jurten, ein gemeinsames Feuer und ein Lebensrhythmus, den Land und Jahreszeiten vorgeben."});
Object.assign(window.I18N.fr, {"Expedition Report · Aral Sea": "Rapport d'expédition · mer d'Aral", "Destination · Charyn": "Destination · Charyn", "YurtaDa · Kargaly": "YurtaDa · Kargaly", "Kazakh Carpet Museum (Shymkent)": "Musée du tapis kazakh (Chymkent)", "Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "Patrimoine textile et symbolisme nomade", "06 — Textile Heritage & Nomadic Symbolism": "06 — Patrimoine textile et symbolisme nomade", "03 — Camps": "03 — Campements", "04 — Communications": "04 — Communications", "05 — Cultural heritage partner": "05 — Partenaire du patrimoine culturel", "07 — Force majeure": "07 — Force majeure", "Lived in, not performed": "Vécu, non mis en scène", "Carpets as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge — symbolism, history, and cultural memory woven into wool.": "Les tapis comme archive visuelle du savoir nomade — symbolisme, histoire et mémoire culturelle tissés dans la laine.", "Researcher of Kazakh carpet heritage · Founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum, Shymkent · Languages: Kazakh, Russian": "Chercheuse du patrimoine du tapis kazakh · Fondatrice du Musée du tapis kazakh, Chymkent · Langues : kazakh, russe", "How we use it": "Comment nous l'utilisons", "What we collect": "Ce que nous collectons", "Your rights": "Vos droits", "Sharing": "Partage", "Cookies & analytics": "Cookies et analyses", "Last updated: June 2026": "Dernière mise à jour : juin 2026", "Legal": "Mentions légales", "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan": "DALA ARBA Expeditions · Almaty, Kazakhstan", "~30 min": "~30 min", "Altitude": "Altitude", "/ altitude": "/ altitude", "Distance": "Distance", "Terrain": "Terrain", "Format": "Format", "Destinations": "Destinations", "Journal": "Journal", "Mission": "Mission", "Contact": "Contact", "Contacts": "Contacts", "Steppe": "Steppe", "Diagnostics": "Diagnostics", "Local": "Local", "QR code": "QR code", "hectares": "hectares", "max": "max", "min": "min", "Max 10": "Max 10", "Max 12": "Max 12", "Max 15": "Max 15", "Jun – Sep / Jan – Mar": "juin – sep / jan – mars", "Mar – May / Sep – Nov": "mars – mai / sep – nov", "DALA ARBA Expeditions respects your privacy. This page explains what information we collect when you use dalaarba.com and how we handle it.": "DALA ARBA Expeditions respecte votre vie privée. Cette page explique quelles informations nous collectons lorsque vous utilisez dalaarba.com et comment nous les traitons.", "How we collect, use and protect your information.": "Comment nous collectons, utilisons et protégeons vos informations.", "When you submit an inquiry through our planning form or contact us by email or WhatsApp, we collect the details you provide — typically your name, email address, phone number, travel dates, group size and trip preferences. We also collect basic, anonymous usage statistics, such as pages visited, to improve the site.": "Lorsque vous envoyez une demande via notre formulaire de planification ou nous contactez par e-mail ou WhatsApp, nous collectons les informations que vous fournissez — généralement votre nom, votre adresse e-mail, votre numéro de téléphone, vos dates de voyage, la taille du groupe et vos préférences. Nous collectons aussi des statistiques d'utilisation anonymes de base, comme les pages visitées, pour améliorer le site.", "We use your information solely to respond to your inquiry, design and operate your expedition, and send you proposals and trip-related communication. We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your consent.": "Nous utilisons vos informations uniquement pour répondre à votre demande, concevoir et organiser votre expédition et vous envoyer des propositions et des communications liées au voyage. Nous ne vendons pas vos données et ne les utilisons pas à des fins de marketing tiers sans votre consentement.", "We share your details only with the local guides, camps and service partners required to deliver your trip, and only to the extent necessary. We may share information where required by law.": "Nous partageons vos informations uniquement avec les guides locaux, les campements et les partenaires de service nécessaires à la réalisation de votre voyage, et seulement dans la mesure nécessaire. Nous pouvons partager des informations lorsque la loi l'exige.", "The site may use privacy-respecting analytics and a language-preference cookie. You can control cookies through your browser settings.": "Le site peut utiliser des analyses respectueuses de la vie privée et un cookie de préférence de langue. Vous pouvez contrôler les cookies via les paramètres de votre navigateur.", "You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal information we hold about you. To do so, contact us at": "Vous pouvez demander l'accès, la rectification ou la suppression des informations personnelles que nous détenons à votre sujet. Pour cela, contactez-nous à", "Four thousand kilometres, three regions, one disappearing sea. A day-by-day journal from the poppy fields of Merke to the shipwrecks of Barsa-Kelmes and the caves of Karatau.": "Quatre mille kilomètres, trois régions, une mer qui disparaît. Un carnet jour après jour, des champs de pavots de Merke aux épaves de Barsa-Kelmes et aux grottes du Karatau.", "Located in the historic center of Shymkent, the Kazakh Carpet Museum is a unique cultural space dedicated to the preservation and interpretation of Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Created from a private collection, the museum houses one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Situé dans le centre historique de Chymkent, le Musée du tapis kazakh est un espace culturel unique consacré à la préservation et à l'interprétation du patrimoine textile du Kazakhstan. Né d'une collection privée, le musée abrite l'une des plus grandes collections de tapis kazakhs traditionnels du pays.", "Here, carpets are seen not only as works of decorative art, but as carriers of worldview, symbolism, historical memory, and nomadic knowledge. The museum's signature is an open-air courtyard exhibition, where the ornaments of historic carpets are reproduced on its walls and railings, turning the space into a museum under the open sky.": "Ici, les tapis ne sont pas seulement vus comme des œuvres d'art décoratif, mais comme porteurs de vision du monde, de symbolisme, de mémoire historique et de savoir nomade. La signature du musée est une exposition de cour à ciel ouvert, où les ornements de tapis historiques sont reproduits sur ses murs et ses rambardes, transformant l'espace en un musée à ciel ouvert.", "Beyond its collection, the museum serves as a living laboratory of nomadic symbolism, where carpets are presented not only as decorative objects but as carriers of history, belief systems, social memory, and traditional knowledge. A distinctive feature of the museum is its outdoor artistic installation, where large-scale reproductions of historic carpet designs transform the surrounding courtyard into an open-air exhibition space.": "Au-delà de sa collection, le musée fait office de laboratoire vivant du symbolisme nomade, où les tapis sont présentés non seulement comme des objets décoratifs, mais comme porteurs d'histoire, de systèmes de croyances, de mémoire sociale et de savoir traditionnel. Une particularité du musée est son installation artistique en extérieur, où des reproductions à grande échelle de motifs de tapis historiques transforment la cour environnante en un espace d'exposition à ciel ouvert.", "The Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent is a unique cultural space dedicated to preserving and promoting Kazakhstan's textile heritage. Built from a private collection, it holds one of the largest collections of traditional Kazakh carpets in the country.": "Le Musée du tapis kazakh à Chymkent est un espace culturel unique consacré à la préservation et à la promotion du patrimoine textile du Kazakhstan. Constitué à partir d'une collection privée, il détient l'une des plus grandes collections de tapis kazakhs traditionnels du pays.", "Dana Erik is a Kazakh researcher, collector, and cultural advocate dedicated to preserving and interpreting the heritage of traditional Kazakh carpets. For more than a decade, she has documented, collected, and studied historic carpets, ornaments, and textile traditions, viewing them as a visual archive of nomadic knowledge, symbolism, and cultural memory.": "Dana Erik est une chercheuse, collectionneuse et défenseure de la culture kazakhe, dévouée à la préservation et à l'interprétation du patrimoine des tapis kazakhs traditionnels. Depuis plus d'une décennie, elle documente, collecte et étudie tapis, ornements et traditions textiles historiques, les considérant comme une archive visuelle du savoir nomade, du symbolisme et de la mémoire culturelle.", "Dana's work focuses on decoding the symbolic language of Kazakh ornamentation and promoting the revival of traditional carpet weaving as an important element of Kazakhstan's cultural identity. Through exhibitions, lectures, research, and public engagement, she continues to advocate for the preservation of one of the oldest artistic traditions of the Great Steppe.": "Le travail de Dana vise à décoder le langage symbolique de l'ornementation kazakhe et à promouvoir le renouveau du tissage traditionnel de tapis comme élément important de l'identité culturelle du Kazakhstan. Par des expositions, des conférences, des recherches et un engagement public, elle continue de plaider pour la préservation de l'une des plus anciennes traditions artistiques de la Grande Steppe.", "She is the founder of the Kazakh Carpet Museum in Shymkent, the first private museum of its kind in Kazakhstan. Her collection includes more than 1,000 historic carpets, alongside traditional chests, yurt elements, musical instruments, and other ethnographic artifacts.": "Elle est la fondatrice du Musée du tapis kazakh à Chymkent, le premier musée privé de ce genre au Kazakhstan. Sa collection comprend plus de 1 000 tapis historiques, ainsi que des coffres traditionnels, des éléments de yourte, des instruments de musique et d'autres objets ethnographiques.", "These are not museum dioramas. Each YurtaDa is a living cultural environment at one of our four destinations, hosted by people from the local community — families who have belonged to these landscapes for generations.": "Ce ne sont pas des dioramas de musée. Chaque YurtaDa est un environnement culturel vivant, dans l'une de nos quatre destinations, accueilli par des gens de la communauté locale — des familles qui appartiennent à ces paysages depuis des générations.", "You sleep in a yurt with modern comfort, eat what has been cooked here for centuries, and meet the craftspeople, musicians, and riders who call this place home — not performing for visitors, but simply living their traditions.": "Vous dormez dans une yourte au confort moderne, mangez ce qui se cuisine ici depuis des siècles et rencontrez les artisans, musiciens et cavaliers qui font de ce lieu leur foyer — non pour se donner en spectacle, mais simplement pour vivre leurs traditions.", "YurtaDa is the name for each of Dala Arba's ethno-village anchor points — and the philosophy that shapes them. A YurtaDa is a traditional Kazakh settlement: yurts, a shared fire, and a rhythm of life set by the land and the seasons.": "YurtaDa est le nom de chacun des points d'ancrage ethno-villageois de Dala Arba — et de la philosophie qui les façonne. Un YurtaDa est un campement kazakh traditionnel : des yourtes, un feu partagé et un rythme de vie dicté par la terre et les saisons."});
